{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down","id":785348,"title":"Panic! the subnet is down!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-13T05:57:20-08:00","id":785348,"title":"Panic! the subnet is down!","content":"I dont know how popular the Subnet wiki is around here but I was mortified to discover it was offline this morning. does anybody know anything about this invaluable and detailed wikis absence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T13:48:10-08:00","id":785547,"title":"","content":"Well, considering that it violated copyright, <i>and</i> people were dumb enough to talk about it <i>on the forums for the company whose copyright it violated</i>...<br /> <br /> It might have been taken down due to copyright violation. Companies <i>do</i> have to keep up on that, you know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T17:05:13-08:00","id":785637,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... so you dont know?<br /> <br /> I've no real desire to argue the appropriateness of Subnet, but I have to say I disagree strongly. A searchable digital wiki is a vital service in this day and age. With subnet and Google I can look up any spell in mage the awakening when my players want to do something, I can cross reference merits from a dozen different books. I played a session without the subnet today and several times play ground to a halt as we had to find indexes and page numbers. Now should people like the owner of Subnet and or Mr Gone have to put in their time and energy into these things? no. They should be part of the service that Onyx Path provide. <br /> <br /> If indeed the Subnet has been taken down then the community, the players and the company are all the poorer for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/duty_calls.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T17:18:37-08:00","id":785641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785637#post785637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With subnet and Google I can look up any spell in mage the awakening when my players want to do something, I can cross reference merits from a dozen different books. I played a session without the subnet today and several times play ground to a halt as we had to find indexes and page numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally describing one of the basic functions of a PDF reader as a defense of digital piracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If indeed the Subnet has been taken down then the community, the players and the company are all the poorer for it. </div> </div> </div>The company is poorer for something that directly obviates the need for people to pay for their content ceasing to be publicly available?<br /> <br /> Okay then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T17:22:32-08:00","id":785643,"title":"","content":"Copyright law is <i>dumb</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the copyright holder for World of Darkness (Paradox Entertainment, I believe?) knows about something like Subnet and doesn't do anything about it...<br /> <br /> Well, then someone can <i>use that against them in a court of law</i>.<br /> <br /> No, really - if I were to, say, reprint the rules for Mage: The Awakening as Wizard: The Waking-Up, and I was taken for court about it, I could point to Subnet <i>as a legal defense</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, normally, the lawyers on the other side could just shrug their shoulders and say &quot;well, we didn't know about that&quot;. That would be a sufficient justification to throw out <i>my</i> defense. However, I could then reference posts on their company forums, which are moderated by the company, that reference Subnet.<br /> <br /> In other words, they would have to deal with it for the purpose of covering their asses.<br /> <hr /><br /> Basically, if it comes back up... just don't talk about it on the forums, OK? If it has been taken down by legal action, it's because someone brought their attention to it.<br /> <br /> I personally have no issues with it (I used it <i>a lot</i>)... it's just that not talking about it here makes <i>everyone</i>, including copyright lawyers, happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:38:48-08:00","id":785723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785643#post785643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copyright law is <i>dumb</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That in and of itself deserves a Like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:36:13-08:00","id":785744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785641#post785641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are literally describing one of the basic functions of a PDF reader as a defense of digital piracy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except where so many rules, spells etc are written in various books, so as a legitimate owner of those now I have to look through multiple pdfs to find things when it could be done with a link and a keystroke. I'm not advocating piracy, but since the company itself doesn't offer such a digital feature I can't quite fault people who turn to those kind of avenues. Plus, I've noticed a lot of times having these types of things available actually gives me a peak of works I probably wouldn't have batted an eye at and I end up buying the pdf and/or book to add to my collection. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:40:08-08:00","id":785746,"title":"","content":"There's always the canon index which doesn't reproduce the text but does provide a summary and page reference to the actual books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T22:06:32-08:00","id":785763,"title":"","content":"You know...<br /> <br /> I personally advocate for <i>writing your stuff down</i>.<br /> <br /> You have a weird Devotion from book X? Write what it does on an index card. If it's too long, write yourself a CliffNotes version and record the page number (for if you have to get <i>really</i> specific.)<br /> <br /> Then if you have to reference a book in play, something has gone <i>horribly</i> wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T22:17:16-08:00","id":785767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785746#post785746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always the canon index which doesn't reproduce the text but does provide a summary and page reference to the actual books...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Canon Index is aswesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T22:45:53-08:00","id":785785,"title":"","content":"The Subnet is definitely still up? I'm on it right now, looking at the Mummy section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T23:38:33-08:00","id":785796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785785#post785785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Subnet is definitely still up? I'm on it right now, looking at the Mummy section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lulz. Now the folks here can get wiser. Thanks, OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T23:38:39-08:00","id":785797,"title":"","content":"Regardless of one's personal opinions on it, I do think it's worth pointing out that if you like the website, you probably shouldn't make a thread pointing it out to the people who might move to shut it down in order to protect their copyright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785767#post785767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Canon Index is aswesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Echoing this sentiment. The wod canon index is both awesome and legal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:28:46-08:00","id":785863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785797#post785797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of one's personal opinions on it, I do think it's worth pointing out that if you like the website, you probably shouldn't make a thread pointing it out to the people who might move to shut it down in order to protect their copyright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. but by counter argument;<br /> <br /> Google Warewolf the forsaken: subnet is 3th result after only wikipedia and the official site<br /> Chngeling the lost Google: subnet is 4th result after only wikipedia and the official site and forum<br /> Google Vampire the requiem: subnet is 5th result after only wikipedia, 1d4chan, amazon and the official site and forum<br /> Google Mage the awakening: subnet is 5th result after only wikipedia and the official site and forum<br /> Google Giest the sin eater: subnet is 5th result after only wikipedia and the official site and forum<br /> <br /> No other fan website is so highly ranked by google, no other website so utilized and valuable. the Subnet is already plenty prominent<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785767#post785767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Canon Index is aswesome!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785797#post785797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoing this sentiment. The wod canon index is both awesome and legal.</div> </div> </div> </div>And crippled by its fear of giving away <i>secrets. </i>How much more useful is a full wiki. ask yourself if wikipedia gave you page referances would it be the consistly the 6th most popular website on the planet (ahead of all porn, news and forums) ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785763#post785763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know...<br /> <br /> I personally advocate for <i>writing your stuff down</i>.<br /> You have a weird Devotion from book X? Write what it does on an index card. If it's too long, write yourself a CliffNotes version and record the page number (for if you have to get <i>really</i> specific.)<br /> Then if you have to reference a book in play, something has gone <i>horribly</i> wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah your right, I have seen the error of my ways. Instead of utilizing a comprehensive resource I should make my own. I will avoid Wikipedia, dictionaries and other sources that already have thousands of hours put into them to create my own. In the same way that I also created my own car from scratch and mix my own medications.<br /> <br /> Now perhaps I'm being unreasonable but I cant remember the hundreds of published spells that any mage can cast at any time with the correct arcana, perhaps you can and if so I am in awe of your capabilities.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you ST very narrow and railroady chronicles, again I give you and your players credit for your devotion to narative correctness. I'm afraid I am not so sure in my capabilities, my players are endlessly making their own choices and going off in their own directions requiring ad libbing and on the fly creativeness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 12-14-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:38:19-08:00","id":785869,"title":"","content":"It's not a question about how useful it is: It's a question about if they have the right to post that.<br /> <br /> And I'm most certain they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T04:02:08-08:00","id":785882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785869#post785869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a question about how useful it is: It's a question about if they have the right to post that.<br /> And I'm most certain they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I dont disagree on that point. Never argued that I did.<br /> <br /> I would argue that this is comparable to music downloads or film downloads or heck, even rpg pdf downloads. A new and better way of doing things have been created in the digital format and the inherant pressure of the user base will push to fulfil that need.<br /> <br /> Tv and films? Netflix, Amazon, iPlayer<br /> music? iTunes, Spotify, pandora<br /> rpgs? DrivethruRPG<br /> books? Amazon<br /> Stuff? Amazon<br /> <br /> Barnes and noble, blockbuster, Boarders and dozens of other big names failed to change their business models. TV, film, music, books all experienced heavy piracy not because people are inherently thieving meanies but because digital solutions were better than traditional ones. I would argue that assuming subnet has been taken down, other resources will take its place, probably more direct PDF downloads. anyone can download the entire white wolf/onyx path back catalogue without repercussion with a half dozen clicks.<br /> <br /> If I were so bold as to offer a solution; onyx path should go to a cloud based subscription model. Integral search functionality, hyperlinks, cross referencing capabilities, additional audio-visual content, integrate blogs, forums and periodicals. these things would add value and allow for greater creator content to be shared. you wouldnt have to give up your dead tree format or even your pdfs if you didnt want to you could certainly still buy them, but they wouldnt be the core of the model. It would result in lower entry cost and I belive would even increase revenues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 12-14-2015, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T05:09:24-08:00","id":785905,"title":"","content":"I'm previous nWoD and now CoD fan for <i>over decade</i>. I <b>never</b> knew we were having Subnet whole Wiki. But I use <a href=\"https://wodindex.wikispaces.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Canon Index</a> <i>extensively</i>, at least once a week. My players also.<br /> <br /> I think it's totally enough with Canon Index - you have short summary, pointing you to the correct book and page number to look in to your own library.<br /> <br /> I even think more - Onyx Path should actively <b>promote</b> Canon Index - that way more clients or would be clients could know how awesome stuff is there to buy and read on DriveThru! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Canon Index administration should only change logo in to CoD one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T05:55:28-08:00","id":785916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785882#post785882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were so bold as to offer a solution; onyx path should go to a cloud based subscription model. Integral search functionality, hyperlinks, cross referencing capabilities, additional audio-visual content, integrate blogs, forums and periodicals. these things would add value and allow for greater creator content to be shared. you wouldnt have to give up your dead tree format or even your pdfs if you didnt want to you could certainly still buy them, but they wouldnt be the core of the model. It would result in lower entry cost and I belive would even increase revenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to suggest the exact same thing. I'd subscribe in a hearthbeat. The content there could only be visible of those books you bought through the service, for all I care, opening up old books/content over time, when they no longer produce much sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T07:38:37-08:00","id":785964,"title":"","content":"It would be hard to divvy up the cash and gauge interest, considering most of the employees are developers and freelancers. Some of the freelancers don't mind doing stuff for free, some are adamantly against it. If you subscribe to 'Chronicles of Darkness' and they start putting up, say, Promethean and Geist stuff when you just subscribed for Vampire and Mage, you're not getting your money's worth. Plus it looks as if old World of Darkness gamelines will be taken care of by Paradox's new White Wolf, not Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> I suggested a gameline-oriented <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>, where fans could subscribe to their gameline, and get weekly or monthly articles, perhaps have a voting system, where they could vote for z-splats and NPCs or new powers and other things that wouldn't necessarily fit into a book. Every year or so you could even compile all the articles into a book for those who didn't subscribe or want things in hardcopy.<br /> <br /> All that said, while game mechanics can't be protected by copyright, the fluff can and is. That's why the canon index is more or less okay, it offers page numbers and book references and an outline or occasionally dicepools, without just copying the book and pasting it on a website.<br /> <br /> The subnet is the one with the issue of not changing their model. They should be contacting the owners of the texts they want to plaster all over their website for rights, or toning down the information given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:53:49-08:00","id":786045,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Just dropping a quick reminder that discussing illegal activities (including piracy) is against the forum rules.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T11:29:56-08:00","id":786092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786045#post786045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Just dropping a quick reminder that discussing illegal activities (including piracy) is against the forum rules.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, no intention of promoting anything but the long term health of the hobby and the company.<br /> <br /> Apart from the amechras baseless supposition and inflammatory accusation of copyright infringement on the part of Subnet none has been discussed here. I would add that subnet had no adverts and no apparent revenue streams based off its pages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785964#post785964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be hard to divvy up the cash and gauge interest, considering most of the employees are developers and freelancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficult but not impossible. iTunes ran into immense resistance when first starting but they successfully talked Bono off the ledge and bought in the majority of the industry. I'm sure something could be negotiated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786108#post786108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, please don't be so snippy. It isn't very becoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just matching the tone I'm confronted with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 12-14-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T11:49:20-08:00","id":786108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785863#post785863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah your right, I have seen the error of my ways. Instead of utilizing a comprehensive resource I should make my own. I will avoid Wikipedia, dictionaries and other sources that already have thousands of hours put into them to create my own. In the same way that I also created my own car from scratch and mix my own medications.<br /> <br /> Now perhaps I'm being unreasonable but I cant remember the hundreds of published spells that any mage can cast at any time with the correct arcana, perhaps you can and if so I am in awe of your capabilities.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you ST very narrow and railroady chronicles, again I give you and your players credit for your devotion to narative correctness. I'm afraid I am not so sure in my capabilities, my players are endlessly making their own choices and going off in their own directions requiring ad libbing and on the fly creativeness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, please don't be so snippy. It isn't very becoming.<br /> <br /> No, I just so happen to run stuff in places where there is little to no internet. And if you can make your own car and mix your own medications... geeze, why are you paying for those over-priced services?<br /> <br /> Plus, the index cards mean <i>no look up time</i>. And... really? You need to look up the rules to <i>ad lib</i> stuff?<br /> <br /> Da fuq? No, seriously. Da. Fuq?<br /> <br /> (And for Mages, you write down the Practices and your usual Rotes. And then you ad-lib from there! 2e is just going to make this <i>even easier</i>.)<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also, all those services you listed? They license the stuff on them - that's why a lot of TV shows are on Netflix for a brief-ish period of time. All of those are legal means of distribution. They also <i>do not</i> translate well to the RPG industry - there's a reason that Drive-Thru RPG corners the market for RPGs.<br /> <br /> <i>Plus</i>, we have to take into account how much a similar model hurt WotC during D&amp;D 4e - yeah, you might be willing to shell out for a subscription service, but I literally <i>couldn't</i> due to lack of funds. Take into account that, realistically, they're going to be getting buy-in on the service from a relatively small number of people, the cost of server hosting, and the fact that <i>Onyx Path owes you nothing once your money is in their pockets</i>...<br /> <br /> Yeah. Welcome to the realities of being in a relatively niche hobby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-14-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T01:17:22-08:00","id":786573,"title":"","content":"How about buying the actual books that those Disciplines/Gifts/Arcana/Spheres/Transmutations etc are in and keeping the writers employed and the product lines going? Seems a more reasonable response than getting snippy that a site that lifts mechanics whole cloth from the books those mechanics are printed in got shut down (I'm assuming since I have no direct knowledge of why the site isn't working). Bitching about a copyright infringing site getting shut down on the forums of the company they are infringing on doesn't seem like a well thought out plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T03:47:31-08:00","id":786625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786573#post786573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about buying the actual books that those Disciplines/Gifts/Arcana/Spheres/Transmutations etc are in and keeping the writers employed and the product lines going? Seems a more reasonable response than getting snippy that a site that lifts mechanics whole cloth from the books those mechanics are printed in got shut down (I'm assuming since I have no direct knowledge of why the site isn't working). Bitching about a copyright infringing site getting shut down on the forums of the company they are infringing on doesn't seem like a well thought out plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have them in dead tree format, their lovely and they look very nice on my shelf but they are to be honest an archaic format. no better than velum or stone tablets in their functionality. So I've done my bit to support writers. I've even kickstarted for some products. I didn't come here to grouse about failing policies, I had hoped for information and support.<br /> <br /> My mistake, Ill necro the thread when onyx path goes to a cloud / subscription model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 12-15-2015, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T04:21:19-08:00","id":786640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785964#post785964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be hard to divvy up the cash and gauge interest, considering most of the employees are developers and freelancers. Some of the freelancers don't mind doing stuff for free, some are adamantly against it. If you subscribe to 'Chronicles of Darkness' and they start putting up, say, Promethean and Geist stuff when you just subscribed for Vampire and Mage, you're not getting your money's worth. Plus it looks as if old World of Darkness gamelines will be taken care of by Paradox's new White Wolf, not Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of this doesn't hold water. The official wiki, could grant users access to only the content they own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like, if you buy Vamprie and Mage, you don't get to see Promethean and Geist stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:45:46-08:00","id":786963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786625#post786625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have them in dead tree format, their lovely and they look very nice on my shelf but they are to be honest an archaic format. no better than velum or stone tablets in their functionality. So I've done my bit to support writers. I've even kickstarted for some products. I didn't come here to grouse about failing policies, I had hoped for information and support.<br /> <br /> My mistake, Ill necro the thread when onyx path goes to a cloud / subscription model.</div> </div> </div> </div> How about politely suggesting that OPP keep an up to date index feature on their site so you can look up the page references on the pdf version of those books you bought, you know that format they went to when it became financially unfeasible to maintain an inventory of dead tree products? Feel free to necro the thread if OPP changes their business model, at least they won't be infringing on their own material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:52:46-08:00","id":786972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786640#post786640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of this doesn't hold water. The official wiki, could grant users access to only the content they own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like, if you buy Vamprie and Mage, you don't get to see Promethean and Geist stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was referring more to the additional material and periodicals. Plus you'd have to have enough people signed up to pay for someone to work on it as a full-time job. But yes, just having a linkable rules service would probably not involve much investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-15-2015, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:29:00-08:00","id":787699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785767#post785767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Canon Index is aswesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when the index is flawed or non existant in the dead tree model which I embrace as I don't have access to the internet 24/7. Vampire for instance I puled 6 books off of my book case and half of them had no index.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:43:54-08:00","id":787709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787699#post787699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when the index is flawed or non existant in the dead tree model which I embrace as I don't have access to the internet 24/7. Vampire for instance I puled 6 books off of my book case and half of them had no index.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... WoD Canon Index is a website. I don't know how it <i>could</i> exist in paper format, apart from printing all of the pages, but then you don't have the benefit of the hyperlinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:44:40-08:00","id":787710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787699#post787699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except when the index is flawed or non existant in the dead tree model which I embrace as I don't have access to the internet 24/7. Vampire for instance I puled 6 books off of my book case and half of them had no index.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you in fact arguing that the lack of an index in non-corebook material and your subsequent difficulties in locating a passage without internet access is a problem with <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>the online wiki containing page numbers for a sizable amount of the series's content</i></a>?<br /> <br /> Because if that's not what you're saying then I would like to forward the notion that you have misunderstood what &quot;the Canon Index&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T16:50:21-08:00","id":787711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787699#post787699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when the index is flawed or non existant in the dead tree model which I embrace as I don't have access to the internet 24/7. Vampire for instance I puled 6 books off of my book case and half of them had no index.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post-it notes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the internet gets invented and <i>everyone</i> forgets how to find stuff in books. Seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T17:56:30-08:00","id":787741,"title":"","content":"I think it's more of a matter of preferring a method which isn't as time consuming and obnoxious as having to go through however many number of books containing in all likelihood hundreds of pages often with sub-par indexes to find some info when the internet provides a method allowing the same thing via a few clicks and on the same page without having to root around too terribly and find a bunch of space for all the material. There's also a matter of those who don't actually own the books but I digress; it comes down to convenience more often than not I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T18:11:22-08:00","id":787747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=785643#post785643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copyright law is <i>dumb</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the copyright holder for World of Darkness (Paradox Entertainment, I believe?) knows about something like Subnet and doesn't do anything about it...<br /> <br /> Well, then someone can <i>use that against them in a court of law</i>.<br /> <br /> No, really - if I were to, say, reprint the rules for Mage: The Awakening as Wizard: The Waking-Up, and I was taken for court about it, I could point to Subnet <i>as a legal defense</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, normally, the lawyers on the other side could just shrug their shoulders and say &amp;quot;well, we didn't know about that&amp;quot;. That would be a sufficient justification to throw out <i>my</i> defense. However, I could then reference posts on their company forums, which are moderated by the company, that reference Subnet.<br /> <br /> In other words, they would have to deal with it for the purpose of covering their asses.<br /> <hr /><br /> Basically, if it comes back up... just don't talk about it on the forums, OK? If it has been taken down by legal action, it's because someone brought their attention to it.<br /> <br /> I personally have no issues with it (I used it <i>a lot</i>)... it's just that not talking about it here makes <i>everyone</i>, including copyright lawyers, happy.</div> </div> </div> </div> The first rule of fight club, is don't talk about fight club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T18:30:29-08:00","id":787753,"title":"","content":"The subnet is no longer down, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T22:02:37-08:00","id":787854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787710#post787710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you in fact arguing that the lack of an index in non-corebook material and your subsequent difficulties in locating a passage without internet access is a problem with <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>the online wiki containing page numbers for a sizable amount of the series's content</i></a>?<br /> <br /> Because if that's not what you're saying then I would like to forward the notion that you have misunderstood what &quot;the Canon Index&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787711#post787711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Post-it notes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the internet gets invented and <i>everyone</i> forgets how to find stuff in books. Seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my post below in response to Karavolos. For the most part its because I play with dead tree which means I cant just ctrl + F and magically what I need appears. I have to rely on the index in the back not only being accurate but actually existing in the book. Loved the old forums back on White Wolf that would have errata and index links that I could print and put in the back of the book manually to continue my preferance of dead tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787741#post787741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's more of a matter of preferring a method which isn't as time consuming and obnoxious as having to go through however many number of books containing in all likelihood hundreds of pages often with sub-par indexes to find some info when the internet provides a method allowing the same thing via a few clicks and on the same page without having to root around too terribly and find a bunch of space for all the material. There's also a matter of those who don't actually own the books but I digress; it comes down to convenience more often than not I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much it. I own all of the Hunter, Mage and Vampire lines along with the vast majority of the rest in dead tree format. If I want to play these games with my group, we would have to do one of two things.<br /> <br /> 1) Play at my place and I'd have no problem as my books are right here along with my notes, etc... but its a studio apartment with little space for 6+ people to be comfortable together.<br /> 2) Play at a friend's house that has internet and I can get access to sites that allow me to search the info contained in the tens of thousands of pages instead of having to dig through for a merit in a book I might have not brought with me because who is going to bring all of their books in their car for 3 hours worth of gaming on a Wednesday night.<br /> <br /> For the most part it's simplier and I don't have to shell out money for a book I already own in dead tree, in PDF format. That and having dead tree format saves me from having to rely on drivethrurpg, which I particually don't like too much, and can instead pay in cash instead of a debit card at a store in person to examine the product for printing/physical damage and get it the same day instead of waiting for it to arrive through the mail.<br /> <br /> That and in case my computer goes down for whatever reason I can just read the book in my hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T22:09:18-08:00","id":787859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787854#post787854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See my post below in response to Karavolos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why you thought it necessary to quote me, seeing as your response to Karavolos has no bearing on the WoD Canon Index not being the indices in your dead-tree copies of the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T04:22:48-08:00","id":790797,"title":"","content":"My friends and I do not have the greatest memories of the world. Also, we like to streamline things. So guess what we do? Each of us have our character sheets uploaded as PDF's and then we do something that is so shameful and so harsh....<br /> We make documents online that have the full descriptions of our powers.<br /> I know, shocking, huh? Imagine that...writing our stuff down on our computer and also sharing that in gdrive and letting the ST be able to see it, too. So that we do not have to look up a damn thing. Not a single thing. <br /> And also an ST who researches the capabilities of his villains and then writes all that down to cut down on having to research. <br /> TBH, my group is lazy and our time is short. It is also sporadic. We try to make sure that all things are cut down and streamlined so that we can maximize our time.<br /> I never heard of this subnet before and I do not plan on visiting it at this time but I see nothing wrong with an index that says &quot;Hey, you are looking for rules on how to do a care chase? Then go to page such and such of this book. If you want the rules, we do not have it on the site. You have to go to that book.&quot;<br /> If something like that were done, then that would be helpful to the player fanbase and does not infringe on any copyrights because it reveals no rules and no information from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T09:02:01-08:00","id":790875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=790797#post790797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see nothing wrong with an index that says &amp;quot;Hey, you are looking for rules on how to do a care chase? Then go to page such and such of this book. If you want the rules, we do not have it on the site. You have to go to that book.&amp;quot;<br /> If something like that were done, then that would be helpful to the player fanbase and does not infringe on any copyrights because it reveals no rules and no information from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing wrong with that. In fact, it exists, it's called the WoD Canon Index (I wonder if they'll end up changing it to CofF Canon Index?) and it's a fantastic tool that I use all the time. <a href=\"https://wodindex.wikispaces.com\" target=\"_blank\">here's a link</a> to it if you want to try it out some time, I highly recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:14:19-08:00","id":791662,"title":"","content":"When playing NWoD, add +5 to any check against becoming Insane if you are using WoD Canon Index. That's how useful it is, especially in books that assumed that good index and table of contents more specific than &quot;Part 1, Part 2, Part 3&quot; are for loooosers. <br /> (Seriously, I hate formating of previous edition books. Made using them a gigantic pain.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T09:11:29-08:00","id":794215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are literally describing one of the basic functions of a PDF reader as a defense of digital piracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except what you are saying isn't accurate. Searching multiple source documents is not a function of any PDF reader I am aware of, and I am aware of all the common ones. Please cite what PDF reader provides the function of making multiple source documents searchable to keep your argument against Nurseninja's defending argument valid.<br /> <br /> This is a valid counter argument:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a question about how useful it is: It's a question about if they have the right to post that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is legally correct, but these two points together, the lack of a needed service and the demand for that service prompting illegitimate providers to arise bring up a valid opportunity for the company who makes the thing we enjoy to step up to the plate themselves. How? By providing a service that is the same but requires accounts that know which books have been purchased and provides access accordingly. Maybe a program/App that does search multiple PDF that are tagged to the same owner as if it was a single PDF. Sorry if that's a little vague, I am not a digital book distributor, but I do have faith that those who are can come up with something to solve this problem in ways that benefit everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...good index and table of contents...</div> </div> </div> </div>I seriously wish these were in more WoD books too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-28-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:56:49-08:00","id":794301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=794215#post794215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Searching multiple source documents is not a function of any PDF reader I am aware of, and I am aware of all the common ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that most of the lines in the series have few enough books to sort PDFs into folders, a given computer's Find/Search function is generally sufficient to the task of looking up which books contain a phrase - my library's level of organization is limited entirely to &quot;DTRPG just dumps the files in the same folder as the rest of my downloads&quot; and yet I haven't had to consult the Canon Index or check more than two or three books to find the right one.<br /> <br /> Humans are pretty good at remembering where they can find information that they can't remember in full, which is why indices and &quot;in this book&quot; sections are things and why note-taking is generally taken as part of the essential skillset for running a TTRPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please cite what PDF reader provides the function of making multiple source documents searchable to keep your argument against Nurseninja's defending argument valid. </div> </div> </div>You've revived a two-week-old argument for the sake of making a petty demand because you can't conceive of using a basic function of most computers to narrow search criteria. No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:20:11-08:00","id":794319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=794215#post794215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except what you are saying isn't accurate. Searching multiple source documents is not a function of any PDF reader I am aware of, and I am aware of all the common ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not a direct function of most PDF readers (at least free ones, most put this behind a pay wall) it is simple as hell to export a PDF to a Word File, and then combine all your PDFs into one giant document that you can search all of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...the lack of a needed service... </div> </div> </div>Desired service doesn't equal needed service. You don't need a searchable meta-file (and you can create your own as noted above). Some people want them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How? By providing a service that is the same but requires accounts that know which books have been purchased and provides access accordingly. </div> </div> </div>And how do they do this without causing other problems? The only ways to verify purchases is for them to start watermarking PDFs again, which was a giant PR nightmare, or start their one PDF store which will require everyone that purchases their PDFs from DTRPG to repurchase them in the new OPP store.<br /> <br /> On top of this, there's the issue of OPP not actually owning these things. CCP in the past, and WWP now, have to make this decision. Even if OPP wanted to provide this service, they could only do it of for their own properties (Triniy, Scion, Cavaliers, Pugmire).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry if that's a little vague, I am not a digital book distributor, but I do have faith that those who are can come up with something to solve this problem in ways that benefit everyone. </div> </div> </div>They did. It's called the WOD Canon Index (and numerous similar projects that predated it). It lets you search a giant meta-index of CofD material, so you can find where various things are in individual books. If you own those books, you now know what pages to open up.<br /> <br /> This is, in many ways, vastly superior to some sort of a high-maintenance subscription service as has been discussed previously (and that generally bombed for WotC). It's free. It's a wiki, allowing for users to assist in content organization. As with any wiki, it can be downloaded for use offline (though obviously not updated after the point of download). It requires no verification services, because it is just a book reference finder; requiring you to have the books to look things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:36:31-08:00","id":794326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've revived a two-week-old argument for the sake of making a petty demand because you can't conceive of using a basic function of most computers to narrow search criteria</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all a demand, rather listing prerequisites of a valid argument, which you still missed. Never the less, your <u>new</u> points about general note taking and using the general indexing power of computer operating systems have merit, which doesn't alter the fact you were and continue to be inaccurate about PDF reader functions, as explicitly stated in your quoted (see above) argument.<br /> <br /> You have my sympathies for how harshly it seems you take mild criticism, that must be difficult.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I have no problems in my comprehension of appropriate etiquette, the basic emotional context of other people statements, or basic to intermediate computer functions. I was using the quoted text as a springboard for my statements, (the primary of which is that if the additional functionality is what people want and not just a free copy, then it would be beneficial for everyone if Onyx Path developed such functionality, also better table of contents and indexes) I did not expect for you cite PDF reader functionality to search multiple documents, because it is dubious that it exists, so it wasn't a request but a rhetorical refute of your thesis statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, in many ways, vastly superior to some sort of a high-maintenance subscription service as has been discussed previously</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms, the multiple points in your post leaves me corrected. Thank you for your very articulate and insightful reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-28-2015, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:14:45-08:00","id":794414,"title":"","content":"Oh not this crap again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:17:59-08:00","id":794482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=786625#post786625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have them in dead tree format, their lovely and they look very nice on my shelf but they are to be honest an archaic format. no better than velum or stone tablets in their functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you lose power and decide to run a game while the cable and net are down. jeesh.<br /> Build your own on your own laptop with moin moin or sqlite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:20:10-08:00","id":794485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=787709#post787709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... WoD Canon Index is a website. I don't know how it <i>could</i> exist in paper format, apart from printing all of the pages, but then you don't have the benefit of the hyperlinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>He said he has restricted net access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T20:33:27-08:00","id":794577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=794485#post794485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He said he has restricted net access.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes his objection nonsensical on its face, because the two resources under discussion here are both online. The inadequacy of any given in-book index has absolutely no bearing on the topic at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T02:30:35-08:00","id":794710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=794215#post794215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except what you are saying isn't accurate. Searching multiple source documents is not a function of any PDF reader I am aware of, and I am aware of all the common ones. Please cite what PDF reader provides the function of making multiple source documents searchable to keep your argument against Nurseninja's defending argument valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly off-topic, but in my version of Acrobat I can just press Control + F to open the small search window for the local document, then press the drop down button next to the searching text-box, and finally select &quot;Open Full Acrobat Search&quot; in the drop down menu that opens. There I can choose to search all the PDF documents in a certain folder.<br /> <br /> So as far as I have experienced, searching multiple source documents is an option. An option I use often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T23:31:25-07:00","id":908177,"title":"","content":"Looks like it's down for good. Time to pour one out. I worry what this means for Paradox. The new White Wolf seems to be getting off on a bad start, between this, and doing a Konami and making slot machines, and a lot of the comments from Dracula irritating people.<br /> I know the books I own I never would have bought without a site like that, which isn't really even a piracy site, considering the many reasons people have to buy books. Still, the Canon Index still seems to be up, and I'm too lazy to check on all the moderated chat games that have info online.<br /> <br /> Still, this makes me worry. Dracula's comments about cracking down on that kind of thing because so many people have been inspired by WoD calls to mind that time White Wolf sued Sony over their Vampire/Werewolf Romeo and Juliet action movie. Citing such things as &quot;vampires drink blood&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":"publicly) 06-06-2016, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T00:59:51-07:00","id":908195,"title":"","content":"Feels like Paradox wants go onto the corporate suicide road. If they start being worse than CCP (remember, the site was open all the time CCP owned WW), they will sail into rocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11156-havoclivekiller","name":"Havoclivekiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T01:03:57-07:00","id":908199,"title":"","content":"Wee... this got necroed...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908177#post908177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I worry what this means for Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means they have basic business sense? As mentioned up thread aggressively enforcing copyright is (unfortunately) built into copyright jurisprudence. Once Paradox decided they got all the IP stuff sorted out, and the new WWP set up, going after major copyright violators is a top priority for protecting their new property.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also worth noting that a lot of studies on piracy have shown that piracy tends to help more often than not. </div> </div> </div>1) Please see the red text up thread regarding the rules of the forum.<br /> <br /> 2) And such studies are most likely irrelevant to the current RPG industry distribution models. There isn't an old status quo that's in desperate need of disruption to convince it to change. The RPG industry already did that when traditional distribution through physical stores stopped being financially viable for any RPG published not heavily invested in other physical retail products (miniatures, card games, etc.).<br /> <br /> 3) Onyx Path and By Night Studios (the two companies actually making books for the WW IPs) have both already moved towards a much greater percentage of core books being available in either free or extreme low cost (usually $1 minimum Kickstarter pledge which you can then cancel anyway) preview formats. Kickstarter based books esp. (the biggest exceptions are the 20th Anniversary core books due to their sheer size and effort) have free plain text versions for people to read; which are still up. You don't need to break laws to get exposure to product when companies move to facilitate reasonable previews (though we don't know what the new WWP will do, it's hard to imagine them not listening to OP and BNS on this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dracula's comments about cracking down on that kind of thing because so many people have been inspired by WoD calls to mind that time White Wolf sued Sony over their Vampire/Werewolf Romeo and Juliet action movie. Citing such things as &quot;vampires drink blood&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is a tad ridiculous. A company that doesn't even exist any more, sued another company over IP stuff.... which happens all the time. And while the suit did have some weak points in it (which is actually good lawyering since padding such suits with as many points of similarity as possible is part of IP law), keep in mind that WW didn't lose that lawsuit either. Sony felt the prudent course of action was to settle out of court (and it isn't like WW had enough money to force Sony into a settlement if Sony felt it couldn't lose in court).<br /> <br /> People treat that lawsuit as some weird aberration (which it absolutely isn't), and a farce (which it wasn't because Sony paid WW off to make it go away), mostly because of Internet rumoring rather than facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:18:00-07:00","id":908415,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_XQdPGV1AJU\" target=\"_blank\">I'm just going to leave this here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:44:44-07:00","id":908472,"title":"","content":"It will be missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:41:21-07:00","id":908525,"title":"","content":"Is it me or did they just copy and paste sections of the books onto their site?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:06:47-07:00","id":908536,"title":"","content":"Pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:03:37-07:00","id":908600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908525#post908525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or did they just copy and paste sections of the books onto their site?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what it did, which is I'm sure part of why it got shut down and canon index didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:22:11-07:00","id":908658,"title":"","content":"Sad, even for people who own the books. The subnet was super easy to navigate, and made character creation easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:41:30-07:00","id":908668,"title":"","content":"Howdy!<br /> <br /> I'm the admin for the WoDIndex (which is now the <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com\" target=\"_blank\">WoDCodex</a>). I've always been very careful to make sure we don't copy anything but names from the books in order to identify relevant passages, but even so, if the lawyers at Paradox decide to come after me there won't be much I can do but take it down. Even if I'm in the right and it is fair use of the materials, I barely have the time to work on it myself, let alone fight a protracted legal battle in a different district.<br /> <br /> The concerning thing for me in circumstances like this is that Paradox / White Wolf has no licencing arrangements for fan sites, and fails to even mention them. I'd feel much safer in investing my own time and money into supporting their products if they just a note on their site saying &quot;Don't reprint more than five consecutive words out of our books. Here's a package of image assets you can use.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:06:44-07:00","id":908685,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11818\" data-vbnamecard=\"11818\">ROMzombie</a> This is for you mostly but posting it for others who'd like to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - I'm guessing they spoke to her and explained exactly what she was permitted, which since it's mentioned, might apply to your site as well unless you already have their consent to post it up. <a href=\"http://rp.thesubnet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rp.thesubnet.com/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:17:45-07:00","id":908691,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a>, that's kind of the thing about Fair-Use though: you don't need explicit consent. As Rich Stim points out on the <a href=\"http://fairuse.stanford.edu/overview/fair-use/four-factors/\" target=\"_blank\">Stanford Law</a> blog, there are four tests for if a work is Fair Use:<ul><li>the purpose and character of your use</li> <li>the nature of the copyrighted work</li> <li>the amount and substantiality of the portion taken, and</li> <li>the effect of the use upon the potential market.</li> </ul>As we pass those four tests, we should qualify for fair use (informational, beneficial to the public, only titles copied and it increases sales, rather than taking them away). However, that really doesn't matter. If a company lawyer wants to press the issue, they have more time, resources and training to do so than I do as a hobbyist.<br /> <br /> Put it another way: We are effectively hard-coded search results. Google Books <a href=\"https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2015/10/big-win-fair-use-google-books-lawsuit\" target=\"_blank\">already won</a> a huge lawsuit brought by the Author's Guild on providing searches across books <i>and actually showing large sections of the material, </i>far beyond just the summary and page reference we show.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Additional reading: In <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenz_v._Universal_Music_Corp.\" target=\"_blank\">Lenz v Universal Music</a>, the Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals stated <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Because 17 U.S.C. \u00a7 107 created a type of non-infringing use, fair use is 'authorized by the law' and a copyright holder must consider the existence of fair use before sending a takedown notification under \u00a7 512(c).&quot;. <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Essentially, Fair Use is a <i>right</i>, not an excuse. The distinction is significant, if often overlooked by those of a more litigious bent.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","user":"ROMzombie","date":". 06-06-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:36:59-07:00","id":908702,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm fully aware of fair use laws and such; Honestly, I believe completely that the site owner could have had a case regarding it - its just really... why expend the resources over something your doing for fun or to help other people? As you said; Lawyers have more money, time, and training for this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:37:34-07:00","id":908745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908199#post908199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) And such studies are most likely irrelevant to the current RPG industry distribution models. There isn't an old status quo that's in desperate need of disruption to convince it to change. The RPG industry already did that when traditional distribution through physical stores stopped being financially viable for any RPG published not heavily invested in other physical retail products (miniatures, card games, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most RPGs actually do still sell things the old way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People treat that lawsuit as some weird aberration (which it absolutely isn't), and a farce (which it wasn't because Sony paid WW off to make it go away), mostly because of Internet rumoring rather than facts. </div> </div> </div> You have no way of knowing what happened, because it was settled out of court. Only Sony and White Wolf can tell exactly what happened. Settling out of court with some kind of monetary settlement also doesn't mean that the case was valid. The case was farcical because almost every aspect cited was something that White Wolf had been clearly violating from someone else, mostly the Vampire Chronicles. It's also just as likely that the much larger Sony threatened to grind White Wolf into a fine powder and the company backed off.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908415#post908415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_XQdPGV1AJU\" target=\"_blank\">I'm just going to leave this here.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually linked that myself earlier to someone talking about this. But I feel like it's still important to keep in mind that &quot;what is allowed by the community&quot; is also taken into consideration. These kind of sites have existed for years, and Paradox <i>has</i> had a history of this kind of thing. While people need to defend their trademarks or lose them, there's leeway here. I'm also not actually sure how much they actually <i>could</i> enforce such a C&amp;D, since you can't copyright mechanics (which that video points out). But it doesn't really matter if they can or can't enforce them because tiny little people aren't able to stand up to them, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11818\" data-vbnamecard=\"11818\">ROMzombie</a> points out.<br /> <br /> What I'm worried about the most is homebrew creators. Is King's Raven going to get a C&amp;D telling her to stop making Princess because it uses the World of Darkness setting and references specific terminology from that game? Again, even if the creators are well within the bounds of the law, that doesn't stop them from being threatened. I mean, Project Vaulderie was taken down despite permission from people within the company. It was clearly a transformative work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:45:01-07:00","id":908751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908745#post908745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most RPGs actually do still sell things the old way.<br /> You have no way of knowing what happened, because it was settled out of court. Only Sony and White Wolf can tell exactly what happened. Settling out of court with some kind of monetary settlement also doesn't mean that the case was valid. The case was farcical because almost every aspect cited was something that White Wolf had been clearly violating from someone else, mostly the Vampire Chronicles. It's also just as likely that the much larger Sony threatened to grind White Wolf into a fine powder and the company backed off.<br /> <br /> I actually linked that myself earlier to someone talking about this. But I feel like it's still important to keep in mind that &quot;what is allowed by the community&quot; is also taken into consideration. These kind of sites have existed for years, and Paradox <i>has</i> had a history of this kind of thing. While people need to defend their trademarks or lose them, there's leeway here. I'm also not actually sure how much they actually <i>could</i> enforce such a C&amp;D, since you can't copyright mechanics (which that video points out). But it doesn't really matter if they can or can't enforce them because tiny little people aren't able to stand up to them, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11818\" data-vbnamecard=\"11818\">ROMzombie</a> points out.<br /> <br /> What I'm worried about the most is homebrew creators. Is King's Raven going to get a C&amp;D telling her to stop making Princess because it uses the World of Darkness setting and references specific terminology from that game? Again, even if the creators are well within the bounds of the law, that doesn't stop them from being threatened. I mean, Project Vaulderie was taken down despite permission from people within the company. It was clearly a transformative work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well there's just asking Paradox preemptively to hand out guide lines for how fan made content is the be handled.<br /> <br /> That'd kill the issue pretty quick or atleast resolve it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Might mean certain things are removed or not put into the book. But better than a stall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:47:31-07:00","id":908754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908745#post908745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually linked that myself earlier to someone talking about this. But I feel like it's still important to keep in mind that &amp;quot;what is allowed by the community&amp;quot; is also taken into consideration. These kind of sites have existed for years, and Paradox <i>has</i> had a history of this kind of thing. While people need to defend their trademarks or lose them, there's leeway here. I'm also not actually sure how much they actually <i>could</i> enforce such a C&amp;D, since you can't copyright mechanics (which that video points out). But it doesn't really matter if they can or can't enforce them because tiny little people aren't able to stand up to them, as <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> points out.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, as the video also points out, the folks at Paradox are probably well aware of all these factors, but if they want to keep their trademarks, they don't have a whole lot of choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908745#post908745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm worried about the most is homebrew creators. Is King's Raven going to get a C&amp;D telling her to stop making Princess because it uses the World of Darkness setting and references specific terminology from that game? Again, even if the creators are well within the bounds of the law, that doesn't stop them from being threatened. I mean, Project Vaulderie was taken down despite permission from people within the company. It was clearly a transformative work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a real risk you've got to be aware of when you publish homebrew. Like, not saying it doesn't suck, but it's the way it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:14:02-07:00","id":908872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908745#post908745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most RPGs actually do still sell things the old way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Most individual RPG book sales are done the old way. But that's because the majority of sales go to WotC, Paizo, and FFG (aka D&amp;D, Pathfinder, and WFRP/the new Star Wars license), all of whom have strong markets in physical products that are not (yet anyway) capable of being brought into a digital product.<br /> <br /> The majority of RPGs are available in various forms of digital focused publications, because the new market place has drastically reduced the barrier for entry for small publishers by removing the traditional distribution system.<br /> <br /> Of course, plenty of the digital focused publications are available in traditional forms (Onyx Path does that), but if you want to read Beast before you buy it... you can go to its Kickstarter page and do so.<br /> <br /> If you care about influencing publishers towards making their games available for free and rely on the market to pay them for more than the basic manuscript, you can do that by voting with your wallet and supporting companies that have embraced such strategies. The industry doesn't need people to &quot;prove&quot; non-traditional methods work. We have things like Fate to show that they do (Fate 3e and FAE were released PWYW and Evil Hat still had a hugely successful Kickstarter for a set of products you can legally get for free).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have no way of knowing what happened, because it was settled out of court. </div> </div> </div>Well no, I know what happened. They settled out of court. That's what happened. What we don't know is the specifics of the deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Settling out of court with some kind of monetary settlement also doesn't mean that the case was valid. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Validity&quot; isn't really an important judgement in IP lawsuits, because infringement is highly subjective even by judicial standards. The strength of the case though, can be inferred from the settlement because we're talking about a tiny publishing company taking on a massive international corporation. Sony could have used legal tactics to bankrupt the old WWP a few dozen times over without it even being a blip on their finances.<br /> <br /> Did they need to settle for optics? Not really. Sony had public opinion on their side because most coverage of the suit portrayed it as frivolous.<br /> <br /> Was the possibility of fighting the case in court a significant financial risk to Sony? Again, no.<br /> <br /> That means that Sony wanted it gone, and felt that crushing WW wasn't a good idea. Obviously it's one of Sony's cheaper options so that could be the reason, but Sony is in pretty much constant IP lawsuits as a company (even if rarely on their creative side of things instead of their hardware and software stuff). The biggest risk for Sony is that WW would have been rewarded part of the profits from Underworld, since they means a cut into the profits of the film and all the sequels; a settlement is a great way to ensure that doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The case was farcical because almost every aspect cited was something that White Wolf had been clearly violating from someone else, mostly the Vampire Chronicles. </div> </div> </div>Maybe go back any watch that video again? Because part of the point is that the individual &quot;parts&quot; aren't protected. The goal is to protect the originality of the total product. That's what people completely skip in the &quot;farce&quot; argument. The pick out individual points as, &quot;White Wolf didn't come up with this, that's silly!&quot; missing the reason those points are brought up.<br /> <br /> The list of points of similarity is to make a case that all the individual points of similarity combine in an original fashion, and that the other product is copying that original arrangement of unoriginal parts. That's what the lawsuit was about. The arrangement of all the unoriginal silly parts, not the individual parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also just as likely that the much larger Sony threatened to grind White Wolf into a fine powder and the company backed off. </div> </div> </div>That's not a settlement. That would be WW dropping the suit. If Sony was willing to go this way, why settle instead of, &quot;we'll grind you into a fine powder so by the time this case even gets scheduled to see a judge your great grand kids are doomed to inescapable debt, so drop it now&quot; because they certainly could have done that if they felt the suit was superfluous enough that it wouldn't backfire on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also not actually sure how much they actually <i>could</i> enforce such a C&amp;D, since you can't copyright mechanics (which that video points out). But it doesn't really matter if they can or can't enforce them because tiny little people aren't able to stand up to them, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11818\" data-vbnamecard=\"11818\">ROMzombie</a> points out. </div> </div> </div>Subnet violated copyright directly by copying text directly. The fact that you can't copyright mechanics - applied to RPG systems - means things like you can't copyright, &quot;gather up one ten sided die for each dot in all relevant traits and roll them.&quot; You can still copyright the exact wording of the text. Subnet provided the exact wording of the text.<br /> <br /> ROMzombie and his Wiki doesn't violate copyright by copying the text itself. Which puts it in entirely different categories.<br /> <br /> The &quot;little&quot; guys in this situation can stand up just fine; when they have a leg to stand on. Subnet didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm worried about the most is homebrew creators. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be. Regardless of Paradox's history, the people in charge of the new WWP have been very clear they want to encourage such things; not that they can actually stop it.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Also, Project Vaulderie was canned by CCP - the <b>old</b> owners of the VtM IP - and was not consulted about the remake. Project Vaulderie contacted Activision, who made the game, for permission, but not CCP who's IP the game was based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-07-2016, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:43:12-07:00","id":910291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=908754#post908754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as the video also points out, the folks at Paradox are probably well aware of all these factors, but if they want to keep their trademarks, they don't have a whole lot of choice in the matter</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a bit trickier. Reference materials are covered under fair use. That's why things like unofficial Star Wars nerd books can be published. It's also hard to argue that character creation rules constitute &quot;a substantial portion&quot; of the books, and that's really the only one of the four Fair Use guidelines that it's close to breaking (unless people <i>really</i> want to argue that an often invaluable reference page invalidates the 300 page sourcebooks it references, and is therefore piracy, but it certainly doesn't hurt Wizards or Paizo). On the Trademark side, they in no way misrepresented themselves or claimed to be part of White Wolf Publishing, and fan pages are generally considered to have <i>de facto</i> protection due to being accepted by the community. If White Wolf <i>was</i> going after them for Trademark violation, then CoDIndex would be just as viable a target.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> You know, it's just super hard to reply to any individual point you made when you break it up like that and reply to every other sentence separately. You can't make any inference about the Sony case other than, simply, &quot;they settled out of court&quot;. You can't copyright a genre convention. <a href=\"http://www.gawaintheblind.com/files/whitewolf.complaint.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Have you read the cited infringements</a>? Not one of them was unique to Masquerade or Apocalypse. Hell, the suit was also over &quot;false designation of origin&quot;. <i>This</i> kind of thing is what I'm <i>really</i> worried Dracula is going to start doing. Suing people who &quot;rip off&quot; World of Darkness by making something in the same genre. I'm not saying that I know they would have lost or won. I'm just saying that with everything I know about copyright--which while not professional still comes from being interested and concerned about the subject, and in recent years repeatedly educated by content creators who've felt it's abuses--nothing in the Underworld film counts as copyright violation. Not even in regards to &quot;how they arranged the silly parts&quot;, because many of those arrangements (&quot;Vampires and werewolves use modern weapons&quot;) are genre conventions. They exist in White Wolf games, Anita Blake novels, the Vampire Dairies novels and shows, Dresden Files, and almost every other urban fantasy series. <br /> <br /> Also, regarding Vaulderie:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Project Vaulderie Facebook page</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We have been deeply honored by the support we have received from you all and we believe that the best relationship we can have with you is that of honesty and transparency. We've received a lot of symphaties from former developers on Bloodlines and former White Wolf employees along the way. <i>Our contact </i>told us that the copyrights were with Activision, Inc., so we pursued there instead, with a pitch being prepared for the company to discuss what we were going to do with the property. <i>This contact we knew from CCP </i>has since left the company.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:48:41-07:00","id":910297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910291#post910291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also hard to argue that character creation rules constitute &quot;a substantial portion&quot; of the books</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why did they include say, rank 5 stuff? That's hardly character creation things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:08:47-07:00","id":910313,"title":"","content":"Subnet didn't really seem to exist to provide references as much as to replace them. WodIndex does, basic information, a book name and page number. Subnet had everything you would reference on the site, entire sections for every x, y and z splat copied into html, even the stereotypes. And all the powers.<br /> <br /> I don't see where the worrying about homebrews comes from.<br /> <br /> Looking back it's entirely possible 'Project Vaulderie' was shut-down because of the upcoming sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-08-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:53:27-07:00","id":910378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910291#post910291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reference materials are covered under fair use.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems remarkably out of context for the discussion at hand. Gaming books aren't reference materials, and publishing facts about gaming books (or other media products) is still limited by other factors regarding fair use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also hard to argue that character creation rules constitute &quot;a substantial portion&quot; of the books, and that's really the only one of the four Fair Use guidelines that it's close to breaking (unless people <i>really</i> want to argue that an often invaluable reference page invalidates the 300 page sourcebooks it references, and is therefore piracy, but it certainly doesn't hurt Wizards or Paizo). </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Courts have ruled that a single paragraph in a 200 page book was a substantial portion before. There's no legally mandated percentage. It's up to the courts and the courts alone to judge if the portion of the book copied is fair or unfair. They are free to ignore quantity of text if the nature of what was cited means that the text shouldn't be seen as equal. A 300 page source book with 40 pages of fiction is very likely to be treated like a 260 page book if a suit was brought over mechanics being quoted because the rules of the game are more important to the value of the book as a game resource. As well, Subnet copied - in whole text - Attribute, Abilitiy/Skill, Merits, Flaws, Backgrounds, and Powers from all books for multiple game lines. They didn't just copy the 2-page creation summary.<br /> <br /> 2) Subnet failed horribly regarding the factor of transformative use. They did not use the copied sections in any shape or form other than directly quoting the books. That by itself would be a very big deal regarding any legal case presented to a judge.<br /> <br /> 3) WotC would argue it hurt them horribly because they lost a huge amount of money to Paizo via the OGL, but they have to own that as their own mistake since they gave Paizo the rights to do Pathfinder in a fashion that was a direct challenge to WotC's plans for D&amp;D. It's too late for WotC to put that back in the bag, but I'm sure they would if they could have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> You know, it's just super hard to reply to any individual point you made when you break it up like that and reply to every other sentence separately. </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that some people don't like this posting style, and it doesn't suit some people's preferences regarding replies.<br /> <br /> But it's a matter of stylistic preference and nothing more. It helps me a lot in organizing my thoughts and replies in a coherent fashion, so it's going to stick around unless the rules change on me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't make any inference about the Sony case other than, simply, &quot;they settled out of court&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes I can. That's why it's called &quot;inference.&quot; I'm taking the facts at hand (such as the settlement), and applying reasoning (which you are free to question if you want) to reach a conclusion.<br /> <br /> I can't claim it is fact, but I can claim that there is strong logic to the inference from the facts at hand to support my additional conclusions as being highly likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you read the cited infringements[/url]? Not one of them was unique to Masquerade or Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div>Yes. And besides the fact that your statement is factually untrue (Lucita is unique to Masquerade for instance, and the comparison between Lucita and Selene was one of the points of similarity cited), this still goes back to the point of making a case about a larger point built out of the pile of parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, the suit was also over &quot;false designation of origin&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Because the script writers had admitted that they were aware of the WoD. &quot;False designation of origin,&quot; is legalese for, &quot;this infringement was not accidental.&quot; The old WWP was making the case that the creators of Underworld knew that what they were making was a rip off of the WoD assuming the courts agreed it was a rip-off, rather than something that could be attributed to being an accident (such as Underwold being made in, say, 1992, which would have changed the nature of the suit and the kinds of damages WWP would be able to expect).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>This</i> kind of thing is what I'm <i>really</i> worried Dracula is going to start doing. </div> </div> </div>Why exactly... since so far all we've seen is a website that was piracy without any real defense. What actions have they taken besides this? Because so far we've got what the old WWP did, and what CCP did, and nothing that the new WWP has done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:37:41-07:00","id":910400,"title":"","content":"I fucking hate copyright law and legalese. It gives a head ache reading this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Anyways I wonder if Onyx Path is planning on doing something like D&amp;D insider, but for CoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:23:56-07:00","id":910418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910400#post910400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fucking hate copyright law and legalese. It gives a head ache reading this kind of stuff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Intellectual property law can sometimes be dense, confusing and even downright counterintuitive.<br /> <br /> However, remember that it's designed to protect the creators of works, not fans of the works. IP law allows everything from music, movies and books to role-playing and computer games to be economically viable. Without it, we almost certainly wouldn't have the White Wolf properties at all (and for various period, we effectively didn't).<br /> <br /> In order for individuals and companies to maintain and legally protect their IP, certain rules and procedures have to be followed. Paradox's actions with respect to Subnet really weren't that surprising given that the website did little more that just republish the entirety of many WW books. <br /> <br /> Although I'm personally disappointed in the loss of Subnet, more run of the mill fan sites are not in danger, and Paradox can still implement policies and compromises to ensure a active and engaged fanbase, including a return of Subnet, albeit in a more reduced form or different format.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:44:07-07:00","id":910434,"title":"","content":"The requirement for it being a transformative gives me a hilarious musing:<br /> <br /> If you took something like thesubnet and ran it through Translation Party and put up the results (not the original words) - would that be enough of a threat to copyright for the lawyers to react?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:04:31-07:00","id":910473,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I wish Paradox would adopt a similar model that Wizards does with the SRD. Have all the info to make a basic character on and maybe instructions on how to run a Chronicle. With splat specific stuff you have to buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2152-phyi","name":"Phyi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2152_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:40:41-07:00","id":910495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910400#post910400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways I wonder if Onyx Path is planning on doing something like D&amp;D insider, but for CoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. DDI is effectively canceled and only exists to allow people that paid for the service to have access to its archives.<br /> <br /> If D&amp;D can't keep up subscription numbers to fund this sort of project, Onyx Path most likely can't afford it. Onyx Path is still just 3 people IIRC. Managing this sort of service would require a very large increase in the permanent staff (and a lot of hardware, and a lot of software).<br /> <br /> Also, what would it provide to the fan base that's worth money? Onyx Path's movement towards open dev and manuscript previews means a ton of this material is already available for free. There's not Onyx Path Magazine to include, as such communications are handled for free to us via the main-page blog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910434#post910434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you took something like thesubnet and ran it through Translation Party and put up the results (not the original words) - would that be enough of a threat to copyright for the lawyers to react?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally no. Translations are often considered derivative works (but that assumes actual translation, not running something through a computer program, which is something many countries are behind regarding IP law), but not usually covered under fair-use for publication (kinda of key here, if you translated it yourself, for yourself it might be different) because it infringes on the IP owners literal copy-right and their ability to monetize their products via their own official translations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phyi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910473#post910473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I wish Paradox would adopt a similar model that Wizards does with the SRD. Have all the info to make a basic character on and maybe instructions on how to run a Chronicle. With splat specific stuff you have to buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes up to the same issue as DDI: How does this make them money to continue as a business? The OGL and SRD would have bankrupted most companies after it harmed WotC's standing in the markets instead of boosting it (the goodwill generated didn't lead to more sales, it lead to more competitors and low opinions of d20 books because the lack of quality control on 3rd party developers).<br /> <br /> I mean, it would be awesome if Onyx Path could give away more stuff for free, because I'm a fan and I want their products. But as long as this is a capitalist base economy where they need to get paid, we need to buy, or there are not future products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:11:08-07:00","id":910540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910495#post910495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it would be awesome if Onyx Path could give away more stuff for free, because I'm a fan and I want their products. But as long as this is a capitalist base economy where they need to get paid, we need to buy, or there are not future products.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that, in order to properly support the creativity of the Onyx Path personnel and associated freelancers, we have to overthrow the current economic and societal structure of, at minimum, Western Civilization? Is there a Facebook group I can join for this, or. . .?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:16:54-07:00","id":910571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910540#post910540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what you're saying is that, in order to properly support the creativity of the Onyx Path personnel and associated freelancers, we have to overthrow the current economic and societal structure of, at minimum, Western Civilization? Is there a Facebook group I can join for this, or. . .?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's several, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T23:13:56-07:00","id":910591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910540#post910540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what you're saying is that, in order to properly support the creativity of the Onyx Path personnel and associated freelancers, we have to overthrow the current economic and societal structure of, at minimum, Western Civilization? Is there a Facebook group I can join for this, or. . .?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, I'm saying we need to do the (simpler?) task of being a filthy rich fanbase that will glad shell out far more than we currently pay for the same product.<br /> <br /> Of course, as noted, there are proponents of your interpretation as well.<br /> <br /> A bit more seriously though, there is a middle ground here of joining other social movements to use the evolution of democracy towards mostly democratic socialist (or whatever labels you want to use) economic philosophies, to push for governments to put more resources towards financial support for culturally vital endeavors (art and entertainment are corner stones of civilization and important for the health of societies) that are rarely profitable directly for the content creators in a more purely capitalist economic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:15:10-07:00","id":911082,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Putting it in a hyperlinked website would likely be considered transformative, actually. I also disagree that &quot;leather clad edgy vampire assassin&quot; was ever unique to WoD. Entire sections of copied merits/flaws/powers have also existed since before Paradox was a company. I've found several of them for old World of Darkness on old, defunct Geocites blogs. As for why I feel that Dracula might go after homebrew--and, also, please don't call Subnet &quot;Piracy&quot;. Whether or not you even agree with piracy, the term still has a meaning, and that site did not fit that meaning--is because he flat out stated during his intro talk that some people have been a little &quot;too inspired by&quot; World of Darkness.<br /> Also, of note, you yourself have already pointed out that in many cases, Onyx Path <i>does</i> give away free stuff, in the form of the kickstarter drafts and open development. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=910297#post910297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why did they include say, rank 5 stuff? That's hardly character creation things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it isn't. Even though I rarely allow it, you can make that kind of character with the core rules standard character creation. More than that, what I mean is that it didn't tell you how to play the game. It didn't give enemy stats, or sample characters, it didn't give you any setting information, other than what's written into the powers. If you're <i>only</i> buying the game for powers, then sure, you no longer needed to buy the game books, but rarely is that true. Hell, I've used subnet for the books I <i>do</i> own, because White Wolf, and Onyx Path, has a habit of sticking things here and there where no one would see them unless they read cover to cover. Esoteric Armoury comes to mind. It's a merit in the<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:58:24-07:00","id":911124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911082#post911082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Putting it in a hyperlinked website would likely be considered transformative, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The transformative factor of fair-use law deals with the transformation of original works into new original derivative works. It doesn't refer to literally transforming the work from one medium to another. Taking a book you don't own the IP for, and making a movie out of it, is not fair-use transformation. The US Supreme Court has weighed in on this, saying that transformative fair use requires the addition of new content. Hyperlinks aren't content.<br /> <br /> Transformative use is for things like parodies, news reports, reviews, speeches, academic journals, and so on. Subnet did not transform the copyrighted material it used in a fair-use sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also disagree that &quot;leather clad edgy vampire assassin&quot; was ever unique to WoD. </div> </div> </div>Ok. This isn't going anywhere because you don't actually want to discuss the nature of the suit; just point out your dead set opinion.<br /> <br /> So I'll go back to the more important point: Why does what a company that doesn't exist any more, who's former employees are not currently employed by the new company that owns the IP in question, matter? The old WWP lawsuit shows <i>nothing</i> about the new WWP's policies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Entire sections of copied merits/flaws/powers have also existed since before Paradox was a company. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and as Paradox finds out about them, it's likely more C&amp;D orders will be sent out.<br /> <br /> However, there's an important caveat here for older and smaller fans sites/blogs. The Dark Pack fan license provided fan sites with open use of copyrighted material within certain restrictions (which Subnet violated). So a large number of older fan sites are most likely within the Dark Pack allowances and would be grandfathered into protected status from C&amp;D letters as long as they don't add more content (esp. new content the Dark Pack license wouldn't have covered).<br /> <br /> As well, both the old WWP and CCP went after websites that went over the line. I can say for an absolute fact (because I was involved) that the old WWP did issue C&amp;D letters and took further actions against websites that were similar to Subnet; and got them shut down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for why I feel that Dracula might go after homebrew--and, also, please don't call Subnet &quot;Piracy&quot;. Whether or not you even agree with piracy, the term still has a meaning, and that site did not fit that meaning--is because he flat out stated during his intro talk that some people have been a little &quot;too inspired by&quot; World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>So, two very disparate points there:<br /> <br /> 1) Martin (note: why do you feel it's cool to constantly call a man Dracula because he posed for the Tzimisce signature character pic, but feel like it's also cool to try to police other people's posting styles or term usage?) was pretty clearly talking about not letting the WoD get pushed aside like D&amp;D did by Pathfinder. He wants the WoD to be the go to modern horror gaming franchise, and the management of the property under CCP has left if very open to losing that status (if it hasn't already).<br /> <br /> 2) I'm calling Subnet piracy because that's exactly what it was. Copyright infringement has be called piracy for at least 130 years. That's the language, that's part of the meaning of the word. Subnet did not have the rights to post what they did, nor did they post it in a fashion that falls under <i>any</i> fair use metric that would allow them to post it regardless of their lack of the possession of those rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, of note, you yourself have already pointed out that in many cases, Onyx Path <i>does</i> give away free stuff, in the form of the kickstarter drafts and open development. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that doesn't actually remove the copyright protections of those products. When Onyx Path gives stuff away for free, it is not an open license to reproduce those products on your own. Those documents still belong to Paradox legally, and Paradox still maintains the right to decide on reproduction and distribution of those products.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see how it isn't. Even though I rarely allow it, you can make that kind of character with the core rules standard character creation. </div> </div> </div>In many game lines you cannot. WtA, MtAc, HtR, Orpheus, and almost all the CofD games don't allow such things with standard character creation. So even if that was a fair argument for a few games, it wasn't for all of them, and Subnet put up this stuff for all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than that, what I mean is that it didn't tell you how to play the game. </div> </div> </div>It's still hundreds of pages of copyright infringement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:13:38-07:00","id":911132,"title":"","content":"Paradox is and always was very supportive of creative content made for their games (video ones, at least). I don't think they are going to &quot;stomp down&quot; on homebrew, because they understand how important modding community is to make games live longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:19:49-07:00","id":911138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://blog.white-wolf.com/2016/06/09/new-dark-pack-guidelines-coming-soon/\" target=\"_blank\">Speaking of Dark Pack.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Recently, we were contacted by one of our partners in regards to the community website subnet due to the fact that it has been re-posting large amounts of our published back catalog content that is still easily accessible and readily available for purchase. While we are supporters of community fan pages that help facilitate the enjoyment of our games and brands, White Wolf has always maintained a standard set amount of reasonable guidelines for said fan-sites to follow (The Dark Spiral/Dark Pack) that don\u2019t infringe on our rights or the rights of our partners. White Wolf and its partners have been pioneers to bringing RPG products to the digital medium and making them available in a number of formats. We will continue to do this and you should expect to see more announcements on this in the near future. We want you, the community to know that your voice in desiring to have convenient access to our content in multiple forms has been heard.<br /> ...<br /> In an effort to minimize these types of situations in the future and help provide clarity on this issue, we want the community to know that we are actively in the process of revising the \u201cDark Pack\u201d fan site guidelines for the community to use and those will be available for the public very soon. </div> </div> </div>And more specifically in relation to Aspel's concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are NOT engaged in a massive internet crackdown or witch hunt. However, when something is serious enough to having been brought to our attention that compromises both our own business and the financial well being of our partners, at that point we need to act, and we did. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-09-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:24:20-07:00","id":911144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911132#post911132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is and always was very supportive of creative content made for their games (video ones, at least). I don't think they are going to &quot;stomp down&quot; on homebrew, because they understand how important modding community is to make games live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Paradox also likes to use Mods and game content as auditions for new employees. I think a few of the Stellaris or EU4 devs were once modders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:27:03-07:00","id":911145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911082#post911082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why I feel that Dracula might go after homebrew--and, also, please don't call Subnet &amp;quot;Piracy&amp;quot;. Whether or not you even agree with piracy, the term still has a meaning, and that site did not fit that meaning--is because he flat out stated during his intro talk that some people have been a little &amp;quot;too inspired by&amp;quot; World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Martin Ericsson also said in the same interview that he has endeavored to make all of his published fiction works within the genre unofficially compatible with the World of Darkness. These are not the words of a man who has a problem with fan fiction or homebrew. The &quot;too inspired&quot; bit was likely a jab at Underworld, which if we're being honest <i>did</i> resemble a few too many aspects of WoD a bit too closely for comfort given that it was a work being produced for a profit by a company that didn't have licensing rights to WoD.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter that you can break it down to a list of common genre tropes at its most granular level, what matters as far as copyright law is concerned is if the sum of those constituent parts adds up to something that is over all extremely similar to a copyrighted IP. It seems like a lot of what you are finding issue with is not a problem with White Wolf, but with copyright law in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:58:34-07:00","id":911207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911124#post911124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">note: why do you feel it's cool to constantly call a man Dracula because he posed for the Tzimisce signature character pic, but feel like it's also cool to try to police other people's posting styles or term usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easier name to remember. Also, piracy is a much more loaded term than calling a guy a nickname. I feel like it's difficult to talk about this kind of thing when people go around shouting &quot;illegal, illegal!&quot; when the reality of the situation is that copyright has a rather large, fuzzy line.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911138#post911138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more specifically in relation to Aspel's concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they <i>are</i>, just that I'm worried they <i>might</i>. <s>Despite what he says in the blog post</s> [Slight correction: He says they haven't <i>authorized</i> any use, which is true], many popular fan sites existed that would reproduce merit lists from various sourcebooks. Subnet never felt unique to me, just easier to use. Googling &quot;WoD Merits list&quot; gave me quite a few hits, beyond the &quot;this is a list with page numbers&quot; kind. The Merit's Compendium fan PDF was useful to me when starting out. Death Quaker's Big List of Merits helped me make a character when I tried trying oWoD. The main thing that I think bothers a lot of fans is that they're claiming their bottom line was threatened, which implies that the only reason people would buy the books in the first place is for the mechanics. It's the kind of thing that can stick in your craw. Even if you do consider this kind of thing a &quot;black market&quot; of sorts, it's one that's been allowed to thrive for quite literally over a decade, from looking at some of the dates on these sites. Hard to argue that it's not &quot;changing the rules&quot; in a sense, even if they are well within their rights to do so.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that when I look up the Dark Pack fan site guidelines, the first link is <a href=\"https://geek-related.com/2008/09/13/white-wolf-fansite-guidelines-are-annoying/\" target=\"_blank\">this article saying how unreasonable they are</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:03:57-07:00","id":911215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911207#post911207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easier name to remember. Also, piracy is a much more loaded term than calling a guy a nickname. I feel like it's difficult to talk about this kind of thing when people go around shouting &quot;illegal, illegal!&quot; when the reality of the situation is that copyright has a rather large, fuzzy line.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>*Laughs his ass off*</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:16:11-07:00","id":911223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911207#post911207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easier name to remember. Also, piracy is a much more loaded term than calling a guy a nickname. I feel like it's difficult to talk about this kind of thing when people go around shouting &quot;illegal, illegal!&quot; when the reality of the situation is that copyright has a rather large, fuzzy line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you believe that, it's a line subnet crossed over without regard for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying they <i>are</i>, just that I'm worried they <i>might</i>. <s>Despite what he says in the blog post</s> [Slight correction: He says they haven't <i>authorized</i> any use, which is true], many popular fan sites existed that would reproduce merit lists from various sourcebooks. Subnet never felt unique to me, just easier to use. Googling &quot;WoD Merits list&quot; gave me quite a few hits, beyond the &quot;this is a list with page numbers&quot; kind. The Merit's Compendium fan PDF was useful to me when starting out. Death Quaker's Big List of Merits helped me make a character when I tried trying oWoD. The main thing that I think bothers a lot of fans is that they're claiming their bottom line was threatened, which implies that the only reason people would buy the books in the first place is for the mechanics. It's the kind of thing that can stick in your craw. Even if you do consider this kind of thing a &quot;black market&quot; of sorts, it's one that's been allowed to thrive for quite literally over a decade, from looking at some of the dates on these sites. Hard to argue that it's not &quot;changing the rules&quot; in a sense, even if they are well within their rights to do so. </div> </div> </div>You seem more intent in trying to get other people to worry they might. You're positing a future event based on a present one, despite the fact that Martin has said this future you're worrying about isn't going to happen and Heavy Arms, Martin, and someone behind an animated video as well as other posters have explained why the present event occurred. Even disregarding everyone behind it, you do seem to recognize that there's a difference between what subnet did and what homebrew is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worth noting that when I look up the Dark Pack fan site guidelines, the first link is <a href=\"https://geek-related.com/2008/09/13/white-wolf-fansite-guidelines-are-annoying/\" target=\"_blank\">this article saying how unreasonable they are</a>. </div> </div> </div>And the mention of Dark Pack by Martin says they're going to be revised.<br /> <br /> Between your name-calling and insistence in some sort of oppressive agenda, you seem to have a problem with White Wolf Publishing. If this is so, perhaps you should take your argument elsewhere. Especially considering you aren't listening to posters here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:44:09-07:00","id":911249,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> It's not really &quot;namecalling&quot;. I mean, I feel like he'd probably like the fan nickname, and I'm far from the only one who calls him that. I'm also less concerned with convincing other people the sky is falling and more explaining why I, personally, am concerned about what this might mean in the future. Again, my first thought when watching the video when Ericsson was up on stage saying people had been a little &quot;too inspired&quot; was that he'd try to sue Jim Butcher, because I've heard many people call that an Ascension rip off. As I've also mentioned, it's not whether they have a <i>right</i> to do something or not that worries me. It's that going after sites like the subnet was never before a priority. It's also worth noting that according to the current Dark Pack guidelines (which actually don't seem to exist on the internet anywhere in the first place), if I made a character and post it on the internet, it's now White Wolf property. Like, looking at the Dark Pack guidelines using Wayback Machine, my Tumblr (and others) where I post silly gifs with titles that refer to WoD concepts is against the rules.<br /> <br /> Actually, let me just recontextualize my concerns: Do I think that White Wolf is doing things that it is fully legally able to do? <i>Yes</i>. Do I think that aggressively pursuing sites such as the subnet is a good idea? <i>No</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:57:07-07:00","id":911264,"title":"","content":"Someone call me when the IP holders actually start doing those preposterous things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:06:44-07:00","id":911273,"title":"","content":"Why do you think that taking down a site that makes your product obsolete and often actually easier to use than said product is a bad move?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:10:37-07:00","id":911276,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> Alright, then, if we can't agree on what counts as &quot;aggressive&quot;, I'll <i>re</i>recontextualize it: Do I think that White Wolf is doing things that it is fully legally able to do? <i>Yes</i>. Do I think that taking down, specifically, thesubnet, was a good idea? <i>No. </i>The fact that they needed to make their second ever blog post about addressing fan concerns is telling enough that they should have at least given some sort of warning or public policy change. Having official fansite guidelines that <i>actually exist</i> before taking down one of the largest fan sites would probably have done a lot to ease those concerns.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-09-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:14:30-07:00","id":911280,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> And yet, the sky isn't falling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:21:29-07:00","id":911284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911273#post911273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think that taking down a site that makes your product obsolete and often actually easier to use than said product is a bad move?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's one of the very, very, very few avenues of exposure/advertising left.<br /> <br /> The decision to go print-on-demand was one that I predicted would be the beginning of the end for nwod and nothing I've seen in the years since suggests otherwise. Without a presence in book/comics stores and tangibles to loan out, the exposure of the game line to prospective players has collapsed. I understand why the decisions were made, and that there's an argument for 'loaning' PDFs, but it's just not the same.<br /> <br /> With CCP/WW making it both <i>harder to play</i> and draw in fresh blood, anything that continues this trend is a bad move.<br /> <br /> <b>I absolutely understand why from the legal perspective</b>.<br /> <br /> I'm also glad that they're reviving the Dark Pack, and would like to think/hope that they <i>tried to reach a compromise/acceptable resolution</i> before tsn was closed -- but I still think it did more harm than good.<br /> <br /> Sites have died. LARPs have shrank exponentially. Table tops have moved on. The fact is, this is a dying community that needs a little TLC, not more pesticide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 06-09-2016, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:25:47-07:00","id":911287,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Because &quot;it makes your product obsolete&quot; is a facile argument with no basis and several studies pointing to the contrary that I can't link because they'd all be breaking site rules. And those studies were about literally the entire product, as opposed to parts of it. Thesubnet told me how to make a Free Council Mage. It did not tell me what the Free Council is, or what they do, or who joins them, or where they do their business. People buy or pirate the books for <i>that</i> information, and going after that <i>actual</i> piracy makes sense. Arguing that the only reason people purchase your product is for the game mechanics begs the question of why they have such intricate political and narrative settings. That also brings up another valid concern: If White Wolf feels that thesubnet is keeping people from buying books, is it really much of a leap to worry that they might decide that the Open Development process keeps people from buying books by also giving them mechanics? Under this logic, what reason do I need to buy Hurt Locker if I already have the supernatural templates, weapon stats, and fighting styles?<br /> <br /> As for the second half, that gets into the same kind of issues DRM has: The answer is to make your product easier to use in the first place.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> Man, it's been, like, two days. <br /> <br /> Neither of these address the ultimate concern: &quot;Does this help, or harm&quot;. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a> makes good points about advertising that I'm sure will get shot down as &quot;but it was piracy&quot;, but free advertising isn't even my concern. My concern is that going after fan sites tends to tarnish a company's image. And even if we do all agree that it was piracy, well, guess what? It still had enough people concerned that they needed to make a blog post about it. Blizzard had <i>more</i> reason to shut down the pirate server and even <i>that</i> got them backlash from the community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:56:15-07:00","id":911305,"title":"","content":"Eh crash lost a big post<br /> <br /> The basics:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> you're continually trying to control the conversation via semantics. Nicknames, declarations about style, insistence on terminology, etc. It's trite and annoying for me. It's painfully clear you don't like Subnet being labelled piracy - not because it wasn't piracy - but because you have an agenda about how IP law should treat the digital market place. And like many people with that agenda, you seem to have little care about the actual content creators who get screwed by disruptive tactics that large corporations have well insulated themselves to cope with. <br /> <br /> You also seem to feel you're free to infer whatever you want and call it implications (but don't offer others the same). WWP and WHW didn't imply people only buy books for the mechanics, but that the mechanics are part of what people buy the books. Conflating it with Open Dev misses that Open Dev has had both &quot;fluff&quot; and &quot;crunch&quot; entries; as well as free previews of entire manuscripts.<br /> <br /> If Subnet helped you make a character, it replaced you buying the books, because it offered nothing that wasn't from the books. Subnet didn't have the right to offer that service. If Onyx Path and WWP decide they want to offer that service with their work, that's their call to make on their own. We should be supporting them providing more online free resources rather than &quot;worrying&quot; about a copyright infringing website getting shut down somehow being a call for doomsaying.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a> Copyright infringement isn't &quot;advertising.&quot; And Martin has actually been very clear that the lack of advertising during the CCP era is something he desperately wants to address.<br /> <br /> The doomsaying about the CofD is objectively wrong considering that they've continued to push forward into a second edition, and have had multiple successful Kickstarters. Less profit? Maybe, but probably better than zero. Dead? Not at all. There are people on this forum that have started playing these games after the move to all digital distribution. They're getting exposed somehow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:03:58-07:00","id":911311,"title":"","content":"From the head honchos themselves: blog.whitewolf-publishing.com","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:31:16-07:00","id":911379,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that it told you what Free Council / Seers of the Throne / Random Legacy X <i>is</i>, because I used Subnet at least 7 times when I was feeling lazy and my players wanted to check out the stuff I could just show them from my copy of the book. After a certain point, I pretty much stopped using my PDFs for mechanical legwork and relied on Subnet, because it basically copy pasted everything relevant from the books that I would revisit multiple times (I rarely revisit setting information because I process it in one go, and never revisit fictions, because I don't buy RPG for fictions and consider them wasted wordcount). Not a single person I know who has used Subnet decided to ever buy a single CofD book after they discovered the resource. Because when it comes for the setting, they can make shit up (making up setting seems to be easier than constructing a working mechanical organism), or they can flat out bribe me with beer and bunnies to read the actual book, chew it, and explain it in about 2 or 3 hours. <br /> <br /> As for Open Dev - they are teasers. Open Dev from Hurt Locker is going to be different from what you are going to see in the actual book. It's a preview, not the actual, final content. It's also important that having these disjointed parts of the system available to you won't actually make the book obsolete, because you lack the whole thing, and often the things you lack are the things that put everything else in a working context. Compare the Mage 2nd ED situation. Did we have a lot of spoiled? Yes, we did. Was it enough to run a proper, &quot;full release&quot; 2nd Edition game? Nope. Too many missing parts.<br /> Also, if your reasoning would resonate with Paradox, they wouldn't encourage and actively support people who are, you know, <i>Let's Playing their, often very new, games on youtube. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:31:43-07:00","id":911422,"title":"","content":"plz delete","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 06-09-2016, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:18:58-07:00","id":911485,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Look. We get it. You think that it <i>was</i> piracy, and therefore illegal, and therefore bad, and therefore should have been taken down. You're missing the point entirely here. First off, no, Subnet did not <i>replace</i> an entire product, it supplements it. People do not buy roleplaying game books solely for the mechanics. Subnet did not tell me about the Temenos or the Hedge. It didn't even provide mechanics for those. It didn't tell me how to run the game. You would <i>require</i> the book to use thesubnet. If you say the site <i>replaced</i> the books, then yes, you are saying that the site had the only material that anyone would buy the books for, which is patently untrue. More to the point, regardless of what you or I think about intellectual property law--and you've done just as much trying to control the conversation in that regard--the question I asked was whether it was a good idea. Whether it facilitates a better relationship with fans, or whether it strains that relationship. And, again, as you constantly hammered on about in regards to the Sony suit, it can be <i>inferred</i> that clearly enough fans were upset that they'd make their second ever blog post about it. I doubt that &quot;don't worry, we're not going to sue everyone&quot; is what they meant when they said &quot;more information coming soon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, while I don't agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a>'s way of looking at it is advertising, even if it could be seen that way, and I know people for whom that's true, you can't really argue that it's somehow making a major dint in their profits while <i>also</i> saying that people have been getting into the game the entire time it existed. Neither argument is meaningful unless there's data to back them up. &quot;This seems to have upset many fans&quot; however seems like a much more valid discussion than whether something theoretically has or hasn't helped sales.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911379#post911379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that it told you what Free Council / Seers of the Throne / Random Legacy X <i>is</i>, because I used Subnet at least 7 times when I was feeling lazy and my players wanted to check out the stuff I could just show them from my copy of the book. After a certain point, I pretty much stopped using my PDFs for mechanical legwork and relied on Subnet, because it basically copy pasted everything relevant from the books that I would revisit multiple times (I rarely revisit setting information because I process it in one go, and never revisit fictions, because I don't buy RPG for fictions and consider them wasted wordcount).</div> </div> </div> </div>I realized later that they probably do write up the factions, but the argument still remains: They don't reproduce <i>the entire</i> book. You can't really use the game without having the book. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not a single person I know who has used Subnet decided to ever buy a single CofD book after they discovered the resource. Because when it comes for the setting, they can make shit up </div> </div> </div>I was able to play all the books I own before I bought them, but I still did. <i>You</i> seem to still have bought books even though thesubnet exists. Just because your friends don't want to buy the books because you own them doesn't mean no one else will. You don't know anyone who uses the subnet and buys books. I know plenty of people who do. Neither trumps the other because both are anecdotal. I mean, using anecdotes, I know many people who play these games for the settings more than the mechanics. Even if you <i>do</i> want to argue that thesubnet somehow completely replaced the gamebooks, that would still only be true for the PDFs, not the physical copies, and even the <i>official</i> PDFs don't replace the physical copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:17:03-07:00","id":911520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911485#post911485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think that it <i>was</i> piracy, and therefore illegal, and therefore bad, and therefore should have been taken down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was piracy by text book definitions thereof. And the thing about fair-use, is that it is effectively an affirmative defense. By claiming fair-use, you're making the argument that you infringed on someone else's copyright, but in a fashion the law recognizes you had the right to do. It's not on me, or WWP, to prove it wasn't fair-use, just that it was infringement; which is was beyond any shadow of a doubt. It's on Subnet or anyone that wants to defend their actions to demonstrate that it should have fallen under fair-use provisions.<br /> <br /> Being massive case of piracy, done with no actual respect for the game's producers (the people that get paid absolute shit so we can have our fun games, and accept that because they value our entertainment over lucrative careers doing pretty much anything else) hard work (ex: the White Wolf Wikia links - constantly - to where to by the books the wiki references and cites to help promote the games in addition to being an information resource on them; something Subnet never did), it was both illegal and bad in the long term. Any usefulness of the site weighed against the material pirated on the site squarely put Subnet in the category of harmful to the financial viability of the brand. I want more WoD and CofD books. I don't want people putting personal convenience over WWP/OP's ability to monetize the IPs, because if they can't no more books get made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First off, no, Subnet did not <i>replace</i> an entire product, it supplements it </div> </div> </div>I never claimed it did. I claimed it replaced a significant portion of an incredibly large number (literally hundreds) of products. The mechanics are not the totality of those products, but they are a major portion of those products.<br /> <br /> People by RPG books for a number of reasons, but their primary goal is to provide support for both the RP part of the equation (such as setting), and the G part of the equation (aka the rules including the mechanics). Even if some people did not buy a particular book for the mechanics, or the mechanics are not their primary content concern, it is a vital content concern to the nature of the product.<br /> <br /> Subnet did not &quot;supplement&quot; shit. It copied and pasted material, and then posted it online. That's not supplementing. That's that ugly word you don't like: piracy. It even did this for books where hyperlinked PDFs are available so that argument isn't even a valid one to make about what Subnet was all about.<br /> <br /> More important, the people running Subnet never had the permission to do what they did, even if it was something of value. Just because you feel like a company isn't offering a service people want, doesn't give you the right to violate the law to do it for yourself instead; even if you don't do it for profit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People do not buy roleplaying game books solely for the mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Great. Nobody is claiming this. It's a strawman you're touting. It's nothing more than a rhetorical lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you say the site <i>replaced</i> the books, then yes, you are saying that the site had the only material that anyone would buy the books for, which is patently untrue. </div> </div> </div>This logic doesn't hold. Subnet can replace part of the book, removing the need for a significant portion of the customer base to buy the product, without having to replace the entire book. So, no, I'm not saying the site had the only material that anyone would buy the books for. I'm saying it had significant quantities material that people buy the books for, which is patently true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether it facilitates a better relationship with fans, or whether it strains that relationship. </div> </div> </div>It's a no win-situation. Either they piss of the fans that actually support them by buying the products, or they piss off the fans that care more about larger agendas regarding how we handle digital material and fan derivative works in the modern era.<br /> <br /> If they do nothing to go after major copyright infractions (let alone the legal ramifications which are significant on their own), then everyone trying to do the right thing to support them by being a good consumer and obeying the law is a chump.<br /> <br /> If they crack down on a major copyright infraction, no matter how justified, they'll get headaches about how the sky is falling and all fan-sites, homebrew, and etc. will be killed off in a flood of C&amp;D letters.<br /> <br /> They can't facilitate good relationships with fans that don't actually want a good relationship (that is, fans that only want a one sided relationship, of either stripe). So they're going to work with fans that actually want a relationship; which means fans that understand that there needs to be a balance between protecting the IPs and making money, and doing cool fun shit for the fans for free.<br /> <br /> Since they're never going to win over the people that see one website C&amp;Ded into non-existence as a sign they're untrustworthy overlords who are clearly liars when they say they want to foster fan contributions but there are lines to what can be allowed - because clearly that's to get us all to let down our guard before the flood of C&amp;D letters clog the works - worrying about how they feel is pointless. They're going to worry about those of us that want to see them acting as a responsible company; both as an enterprise to profit off of creative content, and as one that sees good treatment of their fan community as a priority. Which they've stumbled on a bit, but nothing to actually throw doubt that it's their goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, again, as you constantly hammered on about in regards to the Sony suit, it can be <i>inferred</i> that clearly enough fans were upset that they'd make their second ever blog post about it. </div> </div> </div>The blog post doesn't really seem to care about any &quot;upset&quot; fans. More concern over rumors that some sort of crackdown was happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, while I don't agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a>'s way of looking at it is advertising, even if it could be seen that way, and I know people for whom that's true, you can't really argue that it's somehow making a major dint in their profits while <i>also</i> saying that people have been getting into the game the entire time it existed. </div> </div> </div>Yes I can, because these aren't mutually exclusive. We know that Disney has lost millions in potential revenue from piracy of Marvel movies. That didn't stop them from raking in billions in profit from those movies anyway.<br /> <br /> It was making a dint in their profits because people that would buy a book for the mechanics didn't. It also didn't stop them from making sales because for whatever reasons people still buy the products. This is not a black and white situation where Subnet had to either be killing the IPs, or it was having no negative impact because the IPs were still profitable despite it. It can be both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither argument is meaningful unless there's data to back them up. &quot;This seems to have upset many fans&quot; however seems like a much more valid discussion than whether something theoretically has or hasn't helped sales. </div> </div> </div>So... where's that data about how many upset fans there are?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I realized later that they probably do write up the factions, but the argument still remains: They don't reproduce <i>the entire</i> book. </div> </div> </div>And this argument remains invalid. You don't have to reproduce the entire book to be on the wrong side of this issue.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:24:53-07:00","id":911525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911485#post911485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Look. We get it. You think that it <i>was</i> piracy, and therefore illegal...and therefore should have been taken down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty cut and dry piracy. Which is obviously illegal. Moral arguments aren't even necessary at this point, why is this a discussion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T02:06:51-07:00","id":911535,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> You wrote an awful lot of words about the part we both seem to agree doesn't even matter.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911525#post911525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty cut and dry piracy. Which is obviously illegal. Moral arguments aren't even necessary at this point, why is this a discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, moral arguments don't matter, which is why I'm not trying to make one at this point. I never said it was against &quot;the rules&quot; for White Wolf to go after thesubnet.<br /> <br /> But the question I care about is &quot;Even if thesubnet was providing an illegal service, does going after it the way they did benefit their relationship with fans of their product?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T02:20:25-07:00","id":911539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911535#post911535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the question I care about is &quot;Even if thesubnet was providing an illegal service, does going after it the way they did benefit their relationship with fans of their product?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good question. I'd also like to know (genuinely, I'm not sure how most of this works) how long a company can ignore abuse of their IP without losing various rights to it. I imagine it's something of a balancing act between the two points, for something like the subnet. Did Paradox pursue this too aggressively as the new owners, or is this relatively par for the course in order to protect their new property?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:40:42-07:00","id":911560,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> Well, like I've mentioned, copyright is fuzzy. A lot of it is up for interpretation. These kind of things have been allowed by the community for years, and they're far from uncommon. Suddenly going after something that was previously <i>allowed</i>, even if it wasn't <i>endorsed</i> tends to cause bad feelings. It doesn't help that according to the original statement by thesubnet, they seem to have been very aggressive about it. In fact, according to the original statement, even CoDIndex is at risk:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesubnet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per their terms of service, not even a single word concerning their game systems may be placed upon the Internet without their express consent. It does not matter if this is a simple list of Merits and Flaws with absolutely no definitions and page numbers referencing where they are found, or if it is a set of instructions on a system for their games -- it must be removed if it is associated to White Wolf Publishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, again, is why I see cause for alarm. White Wolf says they're not cracking down on fans. The person they talked to says they didn't want exactly what CoDIndex still does, and <i>everyone</i> seems to agree that CoDIndex is on the level. This sounds like the actions of a company that thinks they should get to own your characters if you want to be an official fansite and that using more than 1500 of their words is <i>verboten</i>. And until we actually see new Dark Pack guidelines stating that's no longer the case, what else are we to assume?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:49:28-07:00","id":911563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> I find your vociferous portents of doom to be exaggerated and actually harmful. Show us evidence of contradiction with what the company has stated officially. Till then? Please refrain from acting like chicken little.<br /> <br /> What are we to assume? Good faith.<br /> <br /> Was there good faith in the blatant disregard for copyright on part of Subnet? No.<br /> <br /> You've been linked multiple times to the official statement by WWP, yet continue to harp on the other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-10-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T04:13:25-07:00","id":911566,"title":"","content":"How much hard would have it been for the subnet to actually ASK for the goddamn permission? <br /> <br /> I have personally asked for such a permission when I wanted to make an application for character creation and publish it over the internet. yes, with merits, and reprints of the book. And you know what? They gave me that permission. Free of charge as well as long as I'm not making any profits and I don't copy more than 3,000 words from a single book, which is rather easy for most of mechanical things. I have long since dropped the idea/project, and at the moment I'd have to go out to them and ask for it again, but still - it's possible. <br /> <br /> So yeah, subnet should die, and be reborn if they start working with the Whitewolf/paradox. As should any other place which clearly breaches fair use. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T04:45:29-07:00","id":911575,"title":"","content":"It *did* tell you what Temenos is, and it probably did tell you what Hedge is. Aside of character creation stuff, it had a big ass &quot;Roleplaying&quot; tab with a lot of vital setting information in there. Sure, it was incomplete, but it was complete enough to the point where you could run a game of it or become acquainted with the product the point of deciding that buying a book is bad deal, because difference between what you had there and what you would get in the book wasn't worth spending cash worth of a new video game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:43:56-07:00","id":911590,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> Are you just going to keep calling me Chicken Little, or what? I'd like to know before I bother engaging with you if it'll actually result in a meaningful conversation.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar294_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"294\" data-vbnamecard=\"294\">Griautis</a> I'd assume they did ask. The original message they put up seems to imply they asked what they could get away with, and they were told not even doing what CoDIndex does would be allowed.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> I never actually saw anything like that. Plus, I feel like &quot;you could learn you don't like the product&quot; is a really bad argument from a consumer advocacy stance in the first place, since it implies you should buy a product and be stuck with it even if you don't like it; but again, whether they had a right or not is irrelevant to the conversation I'm trying to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:57:33-07:00","id":911596,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;deciding I don't like the product&quot;, it's &quot;If I can have my pizza with all the ingredients minus one for free, why should I pay for one non critical ingredient&quot;. And if you didn't see it, then well, it's not my fault you didn't actually read the site in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:58:52-07:00","id":911597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> Did you read my bit about good faith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:16:03-07:00","id":911604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911535#post911535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the question I care about is &quot;Even if thesubnet was providing an illegal service, does going after it the way they did benefit their relationship with fans of their product?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering if they don't go after subnet, they're effectively taking a step towards giving up rights to defend their products, yes. Some fans may be miffed, but without it there's nothing to be fans of and products can continue being made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:12:44-07:00","id":911629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911604#post911604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering if they don't go after subnet, they're effectively taking a step towards giving up rights to defend their products, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What's the norm for the community&quot; is a thing that has to be taken into account here. Thesubnet was up for quite some time. Sites like it have existed since Geocities was a thing. I get that the company is technically new, but it's still stepping in, seeing a thing that was previously left alone, and then shutting it down. For what it's worth, a quick Google search tells me there's a D&amp;D 4e wiki, which as far as I'm aware didn't even have an OGL to explicitly allow that sort of thing. It copies the text of things, gives character creation, character <i>advancement</i> (which if I recall was not even allowed under OGL, which is why d20srd doesn't have it), and doesn't even list page numbers. It has 4,049 pages, and I don't even see a copyright disclaimer anywhere. Sites like this are at the very least tolerated amongst the community.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also I feel the notion that revenue is being lost is a facile one with no basis or data to back it up, but since linking to studies on the actual verifiable and data backed effects of piracy on both small and large companies would probably be against forum rules, I'll just point to the success of the Patreon model as evidence that &quot;if you can get it for free why would you pay for it&quot; is an inherently oversimplified false dichotomy of an argument. Also the fact that internet porn somehow still exists even when it is literally the easiest thing ever to find and the thing finally driving those companies out of business doesn't seem to be <i>piracy</i> so much as <i>competition</i> now that anyone with a camera and genitals can do what they do. Oh, and the success of Humble Bundle.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:50:52-07:00","id":911648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911539#post911539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a good question. I'd also like to know (genuinely, I'm not sure how most of this works) how long a company can ignore abuse of their IP without losing various rights to it. I imagine it's something of a balancing act between the two points, for something like the subnet. Did Paradox pursue this too aggressively as the new owners, or is this relatively par for the course in order to protect their new property?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't lose your copyright if you don't enforce it. As a copyright owner, you're free to decide whether to go after people infringing on your copyrights or not. If you don't enforce your copyright, then infringers might get bolder with what they do about it. But legally, you can still take them to court if you decide to do so.<br /> <br /> It's explicitly trademarks where not actively defending your trademark can lead you to legally losing the trademark. Trademark and copyright are two very different types of intellectual property and protected very differently under the law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:21:20-07:00","id":911668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911629#post911629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I feel the notion that revenue is being lost is a facile one with no basis or data to back it up, but since linking to studies on the actual verifiable and data backed effects of piracy on both small and large companies would probably be against forum rules, I'll just point to the success of the Patreon model as evidence that &quot;if you can get it for free why would you pay for it&quot; is an inherently oversimplified false dichotomy of an argument. Also the fact that internet porn somehow still exists even when it is literally the easiest thing ever to find and the thing finally driving those companies out of business doesn't seem to be <i>piracy</i> so much as <i>competition</i> now that anyone with a camera and genitals can do what they do. Oh, and the success of Humble Bundle.[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>Offering things via Patreon isn't any more free than offering it via Kickstarter, and offering them up for charity as with Humble Bundle isn't the same as just copying books and making them widely available. Larger companies in the porn industry have survived the widespread piracy of their work by buying up many of the alternative routes used to share their product, such as Porntube. And considering your overblown reaction to a completely legal and justified protection of their rights, I'm sure such a buyout would result in a similar overreaction from a few miffed fans. Even then, we're left with bias and an agenda, as you have reason to try to justify piracy due to your contribution to it on the World of Darkness General.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:36:45-07:00","id":911756,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Aren't you just as guilty of bias? At least I've got some kind of factual basis for my bias, instead of just sticking with asking no questions. We get it. It was illegal. White Wolf is within their full legal rights to do something. No one, not even me, has been debating that fact. The question that I repeatedly ask is &quot;<i>was it wise?</i>&quot; and no one really seems interested in discussing that reasonably. Instead, everyone wants to point out that revenue was lost. That is not a statement backed by evidence. It's an <i>assumption</i>. You <i>assume</i> that revenue was lost. I, on the other hand, do not feel that is likely. I feel that way based on the repeated studies I've read. It comes from researching data collected by companies like Netflix and Valve, reading official studies by media groups, and is informed by a lot more than whether or not I contribute to a 4chan thread that you also clearly post in.<br /> <br /> If you feel they were losing <i>so</i> much money that they had to step in and stop a massive leak to keep from going under, fine. Fine, I'll buy that you feel that way. Personally? I feel they did something they're completely within their legal bounds to do, but had zero actual reason to do so, and I feel that it hurts their standing with the community. These kind of sites have always existed for roleplaying games. Shutting one down and saying &quot;no, this thing you're all used to is not allowed&quot;--<i>whether or not they're legally in their right to do so</i>--is not something that people tend to enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:51:12-07:00","id":911764,"title":"","content":"I fail to see how it how taking down the subbet does anything other than foster better relations between White Wolf and the community, considering what the subnet was doing demonstrated a profound disrespect for the freelancers that worked on the products they stole. Not just in terms of diminishing the salability of their work but also in terms of the <i>way</i> they cherry picked it. The emphasis on mechanics clearly communicated what their sole purpose for harvesting content was, effectively dismissing out of hand anything that didn't have dice attached to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:53:33-07:00","id":911767,"title":"","content":"They did have reason to do so. Protecting their rights to the IP. That was probably a more significant motivating factor than any revinue that may or may not have been lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:53:45-07:00","id":911768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911756#post911756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Aren't you just as guilty of bias? At least I've got some kind of factual basis for my bias, instead of just sticking with asking no questions. We get it. It was illegal. White Wolf is within their full legal rights to do something. No one, not even me, has been debating that fact. The question that I repeatedly ask is &quot;<i>was it wise?</i>&quot; and no one really seems interested in discussing that reasonably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking if it was wise is simply baffling. Let them have done nothing, and I could have made my Sorcerer: The Magicking and point out at Subnet and this very thread to get away with outright copying Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:48:16-07:00","id":911800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aren't you just as guilty of bias? At least I've got some kind of factual basis for my bias, instead of just sticking with asking no questions. </div> </div> </div>What White Wolf publishing does to crackdown on pirates doesn't affect me at all, so no, I'm not 'just as guilty' of bias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We get it. It was illegal. White Wolf is within their full legal rights to do something. No one, not even me, has been debating that fact. The question that I repeatedly ask is &quot;was it wise?&quot; and no one really seems interested in discussing that reasonably. Instead, everyone wants to point out that revenue was lost. That is not a statement backed by evidence. It's an assumption. You assume that revenue was lost. I, on the other hand, do not feel that is likely. I feel that way based on the repeated studies I've read. It comes from researching data collected by companies like Netflix and Valve, reading official studies by media groups, and is informed by a lot more than whether or not I contribute to a 4chan thread that you also clearly post in. </div> </div> </div>What you're doing is making the same assumptions you decry others for. You know Netflix is not the same as White Wolf or Onyx Path, that they do not own the majority of what their site puts out and profit from it regardless. If you want to point to Valve for justification, then you'll know Newell has stated his belief that piracy is about convenience, and not price, and undercutting the ability of DriveThruRPG to deliver goods by offering them free on a website is the kind of thing he refers to. But for all you know they're doing it so they can offer some online variant. That they're planning on giving Dark Pack more freedom, things that would be in direct competition with things like subnet.<br /> <br /> The question you've repeatedly asked is easily answered with a yes. If one site that has been illegally pirating their work has to remove their pirated work so the company can maintain its rights, then yes, it's a wise move to make sure that site removes it so they can continue to have control over the IP. Subnet should be able to come up again once the new Dark Pack system is in place, or not if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you feel they were losing so much money that they had to step in and stop a massive leak to keep from going under, fine. Fine, I'll buy that you feel that way. Personally? I feel they did something they're completely within their legal bounds to do, but had zero actual reason to do so, and I feel that it hurts their standing with the community. These kind of sites have always existed for roleplaying games. Shutting one down and saying &quot;no, this thing you're all used to is not allowed&quot;--whether or not they're legally in their right to do so--is not something that people tend to enjoy. </div> </div> </div>Few people here seem to mind, appreciating why it was done. You seem intent on trying to get other people up in arms about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:03:17-07:00","id":911809,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> points out, you don't lose your IP if you don't stamp out copyright infringement. <a href=\"http://www.hypergridbusiness.com/2011/08/how-to-lose-your-copyright-in-three-easy-steps/\" target=\"_blank\">Copyright stays unless you sell it, did it for hire, or die</a>. And the blog mentioned copyright, not trademark infringement.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> Again, saying they &quot;stole&quot; something is misleading and loaded, and there's no way of verifying that statement. As an aside, in writing a submission to become a freelancer, I found it a lot harder than when I was writing my personal homebrew the week before and could look things up on the subnet.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> And? Last week you could have done just that. You posted in this thread on 12-14-2015, at 07:38 AM, so you were aware of the site for the better part of a year. You're having a discussion on internet piracy, so clearly you're aware of what that is. It's also not too much of a stretch to assume you know how to Google something, since this is 2016. I'm also going to assume that despite all that, you've still either purchased or at the very least plan to purchase the books. So I'm not really sure what your argument is.<br /> <br /> Or are you not saying that you could make a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sorcerer_Revised_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer</a> character, but that you could make a game called Sorcerer: The Magicking, and then pointed to thesubnet as justification for your copyright violation? Because that's an entirely different subject entirely. First, as what I linked to Charlquin points out, you don't lose your right to sue for copyright violation no matter how many times your product is pirated. Beyond that, your homebrew would be just as protected as any other. Hell, <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/146958/Katanas--Trenchcoats-Episode-1-Welcome-to-Darkest-Vancouver-PREMIUM-EDITION\" target=\"_blank\">this is also protected</a> due to being parody, and even had White Wolf writers write for it. So, sure, go ahead and make <b>Sorcerer: The Magicking</b>. You don't need to point to some other thing being allowed for you to get away with that, and on top of that, even if your <b>Sorcerer: The Magicking</b> <i>were</i> a copyright violation (say it just copied whole texts from Mage and used the same setting, or was like <a href=\"https://www.rpg.net/reviews/archive/15/15765.phtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vampire: Undeath</b></a>), they could still go after you even if they didn't go after other similar IP infringement. In fact, in a hypothetical scenario where <i>literally everyone</i> was infringing upon an IP, the IP holders would still be legally able to go after <i>one specific</i> person for copyright violation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Doesn't really effect me, either, beyond making it a little more difficult for me to find things, but I'm still biased. I also don't think that they plan to offer a variant, and doubt they planned to update the Dark Pack guidelines until they started hearing fan concerns rolling in--which, again, is something they personally said on their blog, not me making leaps of logic; &quot;<i>Dear Concerned Fans</i>&quot; it starts. Newell's view is that piracy is competition, and you have to be better than the competition. Thesubnet was more convenient than the books. A hypothetical Valve response (from back when Valve seemed to actually care about things) would be to make the books easier to use. Charlaquin and WHW and others have talked about how invaluable the CoDIndex is. That's because White Wolf books are edited in a way with no rhyme or reason. Merits are shoved in the middle of fluff sections. If you never ran a game with Ephemeral Entities, you may never have known Esoteric Armoury existed. If you never cared about &quot;canon&quot; city examples, you may never have known there were rules for a sixth Vampire clan (though I'll admit that the Jiangshi shouldn't be in the opening chapter; that would give the wrong impression about them). Also, again, they wouldn't lose their IP if they allowed thesubnet to continue existing. Copyright is not trademarks. Worth noting also is that this necro'd thread is not the sum total of all discussion about the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-10-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:38:59-07:00","id":911826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911809#post911809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> points out, you don't lose your IP if you don't stamp out copyright infringement. <a href=\"http://www.hypergridbusiness.com/2011/08/how-to-lose-your-copyright-in-three-easy-steps/\" target=\"_blank\">Copyright stays unless you sell it, did it for hire, or die</a>. And the blog mentioned copyright, not trademark infringement.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> Again, saying they &quot;stole&quot; something is misleading and loaded, and there's no way of verifying that statement. As an aside, in writing a submission to become a freelancer, I found it a lot harder than when I was writing my personal homebrew the week before and could look things up on the subnet.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> And? Last week you could have done just that. You posted in this thread on 12-14-2015, at 07:38 AM, so you were aware of the site for the better part of a year. You're having a discussion on internet piracy, so clearly you're aware of what that is. It's also not too much of a stretch to assume you know how to Google something, since this is 2016. I'm also going to assume that despite all that, you've still either purchased or at the very least plan to purchase the books. So I'm not really sure what your argument is.<br /> <br /> Or are you not saying that you could make a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sorcerer_Revised_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer</a> character, but that you could make a game called Sorcerer: The Magicking, and then pointed to thesubnet as justification for your copyright violation? Because that's an entirely different subject entirely. First, as what I linked to Charlquin points out, you don't lose your right to sue for copyright violation no matter how many times your product is pirated. Beyond that, your homebrew would be just as protected as any other. Hell, <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/146958/Katanas--Trenchcoats-Episode-1-Welcome-to-Darkest-Vancouver-PREMIUM-EDITION\" target=\"_blank\">this is also protected</a> due to being parody, and even had White Wolf writers write for it. So, sure, go ahead and make <b>Sorcerer: The Magicking</b>. You don't need to point to some other thing being allowed for you to get away with that, and on top of that, even if your <b>Sorcerer: The Magicking</b> <i>were</i> a copyright violation (say it just copied whole texts from Mage and used the same setting, or was like <a href=\"https://www.rpg.net/reviews/archive/15/15765.phtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vampire: Undeath</b></a>), they could still go after you even if they didn't go after other similar IP infringement. In fact, in a hypothetical scenario where <i>literally everyone</i> was infringing upon an IP, the IP holders would still be legally able to go after <i>one specific</i> person for copyright violation.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is technically true, it's also not the entire truth.<br /> <br /> 'To be fair, the level of enforcement or protection you\u2019ve provided a work can be a factor in how much damages are awarded. For example, if a photo you took has been circulating widely for years with no action and you sue one user of the work, that would mitigate the market value of the work, the damage the infringement could have done and how the court feels about the infringement itself. All of these things can affect the final judgment.'<br /> <br /> As you've been told, people don't defend their copyright for fun, but because they have to. They will not legally lose the rights to World of Darkness, but their ability to keep the IP will be affected, to the point that, like Ephsy pointed out, you could copy everything but the trademarks. And people have already done this, with things like Vampire: Undeath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Doesn't really effect me, either, beyond making it a little more difficult for me to find things, but I'm still biased. I also don't think that they plan to offer a variant, and doubt they planned to update the Dark Pack guidelines until they started hearing fan concerns rolling in--which, again, is something they personally said on their blog, not me making leaps of logic; &quot;<i>Dear Concerned Fans</i>&quot; it starts. Newell's view is that piracy is competition, and you have to be better than the competition. Thesubnet was more convenient than the books. A hypothetical Valve response (from back when Valve seemed to actually care about things) would be to make the books easier to use. Charlaquin and WHW and others have talked about how invaluable the CoDIndex is. That's because White Wolf books are edited in a way with no rhyme or reason. Merits are shoved in the middle of fluff sections. If you never ran a game with Ephemeral Entities, you may never have known Esoteric Armoury existed. If you never cared about &quot;canon&quot; city examples, you may never have known there were rules for a sixth Vampire clan (though I'll admit that the Jiangshi shouldn't be in the opening chapter; that would give the wrong impression about them). </div> </div> </div>Yes, you clearly have a biased view against the books and Martin Elricsson. You've ignored their long-ago stated intent to revitalize the World of Darkness in favor of a direct message to fans, and you've further ignored most of that. You also have a clear bias <i>for </i>subnet and piracy, which you contribute to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:45:24-07:00","id":911859,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> You know, when I realized I could just tweet something @ someone, I realized there's no reason to quote an entire post. It's also hard to argue that thesubnet was harming their IP. Yes, even if you do believe that it hurt sales, it is incredibly unlikely that it would have hurt their ability to enforce their copyright.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also have a clear bias <i>for </i>subnet and piracy, which you contribute to. </div> </div> </div>And you also have a clear bias against it! Let's also not get all &quot;you advocate marijuana legalization so you must smoke pot&quot;, since, statistically, <a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2011/11/its-official-america-a-land-of-young-casual-pirates/\" target=\"_blank\">most of us are</a>, so the accusations of lawbreaking (and forum rulebreaking) don't serve a purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:01:06-07:00","id":911867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911859#post911859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> You know, when I realized I could just tweet something @ someone, I realized there's no reason to quote an entire post. It's also hard to argue that thesubnet was harming their IP. Yes, even if you do believe that it hurt sales, it is incredibly unlikely that it would have hurt their ability to enforce their copyright.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making assumptions and denying those of others again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you also have a clear bias against it! Let's also not get all &quot;you advocate marijuana legalization so you must smoke pot&quot;, since, statistically, <a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2011/11/its-official-america-a-land-of-young-casual-pirates/\" target=\"_blank\">most of us are</a>, so the accusations of lawbreaking (and forum rulebreaking) don't serve a purpose. </div> </div> </div>I didn't even know what subnet was before this thread, originally, I don't particularly care about it, though I am a fan of WoDIndex. Your insistence to the Onyx Path forums that the fanbase will become upset or White Wolf Publishing is going to trod all over everyone's posts about World of Darkness because they shut down subnet is what serves no purpose. Your piracy of World of Darkness materials does seem a more likely and wise target than Pendragon's fanmade works. Though I don't believe other sites except those 'just like' subnet might be targeted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:10:44-07:00","id":911873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Your insistence that I'm being insistent on convincing everyone of this or that is a bit annoying. At this point I'm not even arguing whether they'll start stomping all over homebrew. At this point, I'm just making the observation that fans were concerned. Apparently I can't even do <i>that</i> without people trying to shout me down and tell me I'm wrong and saying I'm worrying over nothing. &quot;Hey, they seem to have upset people by doing this thing&quot;. Whether people should or shouldn't be upset is beside the point. But so much as saying that has three or four people telling me that I've clearly got a hate-on for the company and rabble rabble.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd be interested in actual statistics on whether thesubnet being shut down increases, decreases, or has no effect on the sale of White Wolf products in the coming months.<br /> <br /> Although frankly when it gets to &quot;you're clearly off doing this thing that is against forum rules!&quot;, maybe I should bow out of this argument anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-10-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:26:10-07:00","id":911886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911873#post911873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Your insistence that I'm being insistent on convincing everyone of this or that is a bit annoying. At this point I'm not even arguing whether they'll start stomping all over homebrew. At this point, I'm just making the observation that fans were concerned. Apparently I can't even do <i>that</i> without people trying to shout me down and tell me I'm wrong and saying I'm worrying over nothing. &quot;Hey, they seem to have upset people by doing this thing&quot;. Whether people should or shouldn't be upset is beside the point. But so much as saying that has three or four people telling me that I've clearly got a hate-on for the company and rabble rabble.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you've 'recontextualized' your purpose for being here several times, and despite that you keep bringing up original points. <br /> <br /> You've stated that fans were concerned, and you've posted so at least one fan clearly is. Then you tie in your justification for piracy.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk to Elriccson, I don't believe he's ever posted here, this being the Chronicles of Darkness board. If you want statistics regarding sales, you should ask Rich Thomas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:39:36-07:00","id":911897,"title":"","content":"Can we stop feeding the troll now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:34:21-07:00","id":911959,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a>, toning it back a bit would be helpful. I think I get why you feel being curt with this is the best tactic, but if you want to go to the point of calling someone a forum-rule breaker, just report it? Good faith readings go in both directions to be successful after all.<br /> <br /> That said though, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> your posts are getting increasingly difficult to tell between trying to be serious about this, and concern trolling. Given that one of the classic formulations of concern trolling is, &quot;I support X, but is X worth it because of worry Y?&quot; I hope you can see why the re-contextualization isn't necessarily being met well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:56:33-07:00","id":911975,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I'm sorry that caring about things is trolling now? This is clearly a subject that I'm both passionate and knowledgeable about, and every time I muse over whether it was a good idea, everyone wants to say things with no factual basis, or simply fall back on &quot;but the law&quot;, as if Colorado and others hadn't decided that at least <i>some</i> laws were ridiculous. You and others can say &quot;but the law&quot; all you like, but the fact is that plenty of people are upset over it. <i>I'm</i> clearly at least a little miffed about it, on top of caring about the broader issues. Something that has been seen as acceptable within the roleplaying community is being punished without warning. I would argue that it's as if the cops started writing people up for jaywalking, but jaywalking as a crime only exists <a href=\"http://&#91;COLOR=#000000\" target=\"_blank\">because automobile manufacturers wanted to blame pedestrians for accidents</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also, I never said I support their actions. I said they were legal. I clearly don't support their action. I don't support arresting people for pot, either.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-10-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:26:39-07:00","id":911987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/785348-panic-the-subnet-is-down?p=911809#post911809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> As <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> points out, you don't lose your IP if you don't stamp out copyright infringement. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hypergridbusiness.com/2011/08/how-to-lose-your-copyright-in-three-easy-steps/&amp;quot;]Copyright</a> stays unless you sell it, did it for hire, or die[/URL]. And the blog mentioned copyright, not trademark infringement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Copyright is supposed to time out after a period and enter the public domain at some point. But legislation kinda screwed the pooch there rather hard... <br /> <br /> Thanks, Disney.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:44:34-07:00","id":911998,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> The Mouse wants his Money. The Mouse gets what the Mouse wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Che